    \ 0.510145  ASW_label: 0.597647  ARI: 0.334002  NMI: 0.606113\n  Graph_conn: 0.701587  kBET: 0.733084  iLISI: 0.373820  cLISI: 0.992514\n  PCR: 0.895223  Cell_cycle: 0.260441\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 894\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been successfully fixed and is now running without crashing. The original code failed due to a missing dependency (`bbknn` package), which has been replaced with standard scanpy functionality.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 894) failed with the following error:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'bbknn'\nImportError: Please install bbknn: `pip install bbknn`.\n```\n\nThe code attempted to use `sc.external.pp.bbknn()` for batch-balanced k-nearest neighbors graph construction, but the `bbknn` package was not installed in the evaluation environment (`batch_integration` conda environment).\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n### 1. Removed BBKNN\
    \ Dependency\n- Eliminated the call to `sc.external.pp.bbknn()` which required the missing package\n\n### 2. Implemented Fallback Strategy\nAdded a try-except block to attempt multiple batch correction approaches:\n- **Primary approach**: Try using Harmony integration (`sce.pp.harmony_integrate()`) if available\n  - Uses Harmony-corrected PCA representation for neighbor computation\n- **Fallback approach**: Use standard neighbors on PCA if Harmony is not available\n  - Falls back to `sc.pp.neighbors()` with standard PCA\n\n### 3. Maintained Core Functionality\n- Preserved all preprocessing steps (normalization, log-transform, HVG selection, PCA)\n- Kept UMAP embedding computation\n- Maintained output structure with proper metadata\n- Updated method_id to reflect the new approach: `'scanpy_umap_baseline'`\n\n## Code Changes\nKey differences in `submission_v2.py`:\n```python\n# Instead of:\n# sc.external.pp.bbknn(adata_filtered, batch_key='batch', n_pcs=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n\n# Now\
    \ uses:\ntry:\n    import scanpy.external as sce\n    sce.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_filtered, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_pca_harmony')\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_filtered, n_neighbors=30, use_rep='X_pca_harmony', random_state=0)\nexcept (ImportError, AttributeError):\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_filtered, n_neighbors=30, n_pcs=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n```\n\n## Verification Results\nThe monitor script (`monitor_evaluation.py 2`) confirmed:\n- **Exit code**: 0 (Success)\n- **Runtime**: Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- **Status**: The evaluation is processing successfully, just taking time to complete\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix successfully addresses the dependency issue while maintaining the core batch integration functionality. The code now runs in the evaluation environment without requiring additional package installations. The submission uses standard scanpy methods that are available in the base environment, making it more portable and reliable.\n\
    \nThe longer runtime is expected for batch integration algorithms processing 20,000 cells with 2,000 genes across 4 batches, and does not indicate any problem with the implementation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Aletheia I: Starting Scanpy + UMAP Baseline (without BBKNN).\")\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing: Normalize and log-transform raw counts\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        print(\"  Using batch-aware HVGs...\")\n    \
    \    hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n        adata_filtered = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found, using all genes.\")\n        adata_filtered = adata.copy()\n\n    # 3. Perform PCA on the filtered data\n    print(\"  Computing PCA...\")\n    n_pcs_target = 100\n    n_pcs = min(n_pcs_target, adata_filtered.shape[1] - 1, adata_filtered.shape[0] - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_filtered, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n    # Ensure 'batch' is categorical\n    adata_filtered.obs['batch'] = adata_filtered.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n\n    # 4. Try Harmony integration if available, otherwise use standard neighbors\n    print(\"  Attempting batch correction...\")\n    try:\n        # Try using Harmony for batch correction\n        import scanpy.external as sce\n        print(\"    Using Harmony for batch correction...\")\n        sce.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_filtered, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_pca_harmony')\n        # Use harmony-corrected\
    \ PCA for neighbors\n        sc.pp.neighbors(adata_filtered, n_neighbors=30, use_rep='X_pca_harmony', random_state=0)\n    except (ImportError, AttributeError):\n        # Fallback: use standard neighbors on PCA\n        print(\"    Harmony not available, using standard neighbors on PCA...\")\n        sc.pp.neighbors(adata_filtered, n_neighbors=30, n_pcs=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n\n    # 5. Compute UMAP embedding from the corrected graph\n    print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata_filtered, random_state=0)\n    X_umap = adata_filtered.obsm['X_umap']\n\n    # 6. Create output AnnData with embedding\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_umap}, # Output the UMAP embedding\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'log1p_umap'),\n            'method_id': 'scanpy_umap_baseline',\n      \
    \      'params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'hvgs_used': 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns else 'all_genes',\n                'batch_correction': 'attempted'\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Aletheia I Scanpy + UMAP Baseline complete. UMAP embedding shape: {X_umap.shape}\")\n    return output_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nAletheia I: Starting Scanpy + UMAP Baseline (without BBKNN).\n  Normalizing total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Using batch-aware HVGs...\n  Computing PCA...\n  Attempting batch correction...\n    Using Harmony for batch correction...\n  Computing UMAP embedding...\n✓ Aletheia I Scanpy + UMAP Baseline complete. UMAP embedding shape: (20000, 2)\n\
    \  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/5d7e01d4-2878-420a-987b-022f98077d6b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 5d7e01d4-2878-420a-987b-022f98077d6b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-28 00:34:54,748 - harmonypy - INFO - Computing initial centroids with sklearn.KMeans...\n2025-10-28 00:34:59,343 - harmonypy - INFO - sklearn.KMeans initialization complete.\n2025-10-28 00:34:59,423 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 1 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:05,356 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 2 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:16,795 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 3 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:21,299 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 4 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:24,999 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 5 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:28,318 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 6 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:32,900 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 7 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:35,627 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 8 of 10\n2025-10-28 00:35:39,018 - harmonypy - INFO - Converged after 8 iterations\n\
    \n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 894 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy BBKNN + UMAP Baseline | Aletheia I | 584 | 0.5265 | 0.334 | 0.000 | 0.322 | 0.295 | 0.696 | 0.606 | 0.895 | 0.974 | 0.374 | 0.768 |\n| 892 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP Baseline | Aletheia I | 583\
    \ | 0.4530 | 0.287 | 0.000 | 0.243 | 0.629 | 0.698 | 0.613 | 0.330 | 0.991 | 0.030 | 0.708 |\n| 889 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy Combat Baseline (PCA 100) | Aletheia I | 581 | 0.6163 | 0.596 | 0.748 | 0.207 | 0.239 | 0.908 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.984 | 0.109 | 0.685 |\n| 886 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy Combat Baseline | Aletheia I | 579 | 0.5941 | 0.591 | 0.676 | 0.223 | 0.294 | 0.878 | 0.692 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.057 | 0.543 |\n| 885 | 1 | Aletheia I - Mean Center PCA Baseline | Aletheia I | 578 | 0.5716 | 0.457 | 0.640 | 0.220 | 0.303 | 0.876 | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.989 | 0.012 | 0.553 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation &\
