- text: "My previous submission failed again because of an underscore in the tag \"aletheia_i\". I apologize for this oversight. I will correct the tag to \"aletheia i\" and resubmit the code for \"Aletheia I - Combat + Harmony + UMAP\" workflow.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - Combat + Harmony + UMAP\"\ntags: \"combat, harmony, scanpy, umap, embedding, aletheia i\"\nabstract: \"A refined batch integration strategy combining Combat correction with Harmony integration and UMAP embedding. After standard preprocessing (normalization, log-transformation, HVG selection), `scanpy.pp.combat` is applied. PCA (100 components) is then computed, followed by `scanpy.external.pp.harmony_integrate` on the Combat-corrected PCA space. Finally, nearest neighbors and UMAP embedding are derived from the Harmony-corrected space, aiming for a robust balance of batch mixing and biological preservation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy\
    \ as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  import scanpy.external as sce # Import scanpy.external for Harmony\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Starting Combat + Harmony + UMAP workflow.\")\n\n      # 1. Preprocessing: Normalize and log-transform raw counts\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          print(\"  Using batch-aware HVGs...\")\n          hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n          adata_filtered = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found, using all genes.\")\n          adata_filtered = adata.copy()\n\n      # 3. Apply Combat batch correction\n      print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat...\")\n      adata_filtered.obs['batch'] = adata_filtered.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n\
    \      sc.pp.combat(adata_filtered, key='batch')\n      # Corrected data is in adata_filtered.X\n\n      # 4. Perform PCA on the Combat-corrected data\n      print(\"  Computing PCA (100 components) from Combat-corrected data...\")\n      n_pcs_target = 100\n      n_pcs = min(n_pcs_target, adata_filtered.shape[1] - 1, adata_filtered.shape[0] - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_filtered, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=False) # Use all genes after Combat if HVG mask not applied to X\n\n      # 5. Apply Harmony integration on the Combat-corrected PCA space\n      print(\"  Applying Harmony integration on Combat-corrected PCA...\")\n      sce.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_filtered, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_pca_harmony')\n      # The Harmony-corrected PCA is now in adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony']\n\n      # 6. Compute neighbors on the Harmony-corrected PCA space\n      print(\"  Computing neighbors from Harmony-corrected PCA...\")\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_filtered,\
    \ n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X_pca_harmony', random_state=0)\n\n      # 7. Compute UMAP embedding\n      print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding...\")\n      sc.tl.umap(adata_filtered, random_state=0)\n      X_umap = adata_filtered.obsm['X_umap']\n\n      # 8. Create output AnnData with embedding\n      output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': X_umap}, # Output the UMAP embedding\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'log1p_combat_harmony_umap'),\n              'method_id': 'combat_harmony_umap',\n              'params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'hvgs_used': 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns else 'all_genes',\n                  'combat_key': 'batch',\n                  'harmony_key': 'batch'\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(f\"✓ Aletheia I\
    \ Combat + Harmony + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: {X_umap.shape}\")\n      return output_adata\n```"
