role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 599\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,114 / 600,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 34 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aletheia I - Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP' (ID: 922) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5101762881078767\n**ASW_batch:** 0.225\n**ASW_label:** 0.204\n**ARI:** 0.325\n**NMI:** 0.572\n**Graph_conn:** 0.678\n**kBET:** 0.767\n**iLISI:** 0.330\n**cLISI:** 0.965\n**PCR:** 0.722\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.313\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.225  ASW_label: 0.204  ARI: 0.325  NMI: 0.572\n  Graph_conn: 0.678  kBET: 0.767  iLISI: 0.330  cLISI: 0.965\n  PCR: 0.722  Cell_cycle: 0.313\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.634884  ASW_label: 0.529336  ARI: 0.324860  NMI: 0.571653\n  Graph_conn: 0.683756  kBET: 0.732078  iLISI: 0.330225  cLISI: 0.989916\n  PCR: 0.722224  Cell_cycle: 0.276118\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 922\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on the first attempt. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code created a custom BBKNN-like graph and stored the connectivity and distance matrices in:\n- `adata_filtered.obsp['connectivities']`\n- `adata_filtered.obsp['distances']`\n\nHowever, when calling `sc.tl.umap(adata_filtered, random_state=0)`, Scanpy's UMAP function expects to find neighbor graph metadata in `adata_filtered.uns['neighbors']`. Without this metadata dictionary, UMAP raises:\n```\nValueError: Did not find .uns['neighbors']. Run `sc.pp.neighbors` first.\n```\n\nThe error occurred at line 130 of the original submission when calling `sc.tl.umap()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the required neighbors\
    \ metadata dictionary to `adata_filtered.uns['neighbors']` before calling `sc.tl.umap()`:\n\n```python\n# FIX: Add neighbors metadata that sc.tl.umap expects\nprint(\"  Adding neighbors metadata for UMAP...\")\nadata_filtered.uns['neighbors'] = {\n    'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n    'distances_key': 'distances',\n    'params': {\n        'n_neighbors': neighbors_within_batch,\n        'method': 'bbknn_like_manual',\n        'metric': 'euclidean',\n        'use_rep': 'X_pca'\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis metadata tells UMAP where to find the pre-computed neighbor graph matrices and what parameters were used to generate them. This is the expected Scanpy data structure that `sc.tl.umap()` looks for when using a custom neighbor graph.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Fixed file**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- **Fix location**: Added 9 lines before the `sc.tl.umap()` call (after line 124 in the original code)\n- **Testing**: Code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing,\
    \ indicating the fix resolved the issue\n- **Impact**: Minimal - only added metadata structure, no changes to algorithm logic or graph construction\n\nThe fix maintains the original algorithm's behavior (Combat + BBKNN-like graph construction + UMAP) while providing the data structure that Scanpy's UMAP function requires to use the custom-built neighbor graph.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Aletheia I: Starting Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP workflow.\")\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing: Normalize and log-transform raw counts\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n\
    \    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        print(\"  Using batch-aware HVGs...\")\n        hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n        adata_filtered = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found, using all genes.\")\n        adata_filtered = adata.copy()\n\n    # 3. Apply Combat batch correction\n    print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat...\")\n    adata_filtered.obs['batch'] = adata_filtered.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_filtered, key='batch')\n\n    # 4. Perform PCA on the Combat-corrected data\n    print(\"  Computing PCA (100 components) from Combat-corrected data...\")\n    n_pcs_target = 100\n    n_pcs = min(n_pcs_target, adata_filtered.shape[1] - 1, adata_filtered.shape[0] - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_filtered, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=False)\n\
    \    X_pca_combat = adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Part 2: BBKNN-like Graph Construction (Manual) - NO TRIMMING\n    print(\"  Starting manual BBKNN-like graph construction on Combat-corrected PCA (no trimming)...\")\n    neighbors_within_batch = 10 # Number of neighbors to find within each batch for balancing\n    n_cells = adata_filtered.n_obs\n    batches = adata_filtered.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {\n        batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n        for batch in unique_batches\n    }\n\n    all_neighbors_and_distances = {} # Store (global_idx, distance) tuples, then process to combine\n\n    for batch_id, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n        n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n        if n_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"    Processing batch '{batch}' ({n_batch_cells} cells)...\")\n\n   \
    \     batch_pca_data = X_pca_combat[batch_indices]\n\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n            n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells),\n            metric='euclidean',\n            algorithm='auto',\n            n_jobs=1\n        )\n        nn_model.fit(batch_pca_data)\n\n        # Query ALL cells against this batch's PCA data\n        distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(\n            X_pca_combat, # Query all cells from the full dataset\n            n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n        )\n\n        for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n            distances = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n\n            neighbor_indices_global = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local]\n\n            # Filter out self-loops\n            mask = neighbor_indices_global != query_cell_idx\n            neighbors_filtered = neighbor_indices_global[mask]\n            distances_filtered\
    \ = distances[mask]\n\n            # Store up to neighbors_within_batch distinct neighbors\n            if query_cell_idx not in all_neighbors_and_distances:\n                all_neighbors_and_distances[query_cell_idx] = {}\n\n            for i in range(min(neighbors_within_batch, len(neighbors_filtered))):\n                n_idx = neighbors_filtered[i]\n                dist = distances_filtered[i]\n                if n_idx not in all_neighbors_and_distances[query_cell_idx] or dist < all_neighbors_and_distances[query_cell_idx][n_idx]:\n                    all_neighbors_and_distances[query_cell_idx][n_idx] = dist\n\n    print(\"  Creating connectivity and distance matrices...\")\n\n    distances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx, neighbors_map in all_neighbors_and_distances.items():\n        for n_idx, dist in neighbors_map.items():\n            distances_matrix[cell_idx, n_idx] = dist\n\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.tocsr()\n   \
    \ distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T) # Symmetrize\n\n    connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n\n    # Apply Gaussian kernel for connectivity weights\n    if connectivities_matrix.data.size > 0: # Check if there is any data to process\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                # Use median distance as bandwidth\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T) # Symmetrize again\n\n    # Store the generated graph in adata_filtered\n    adata_filtered.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = connectivities_matrix.astype(np.float32)\n    adata_filtered.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # FIX: Add neighbors metadata that sc.tl.umap expects\n    print(\"  Adding neighbors metadata for UMAP...\")\n    adata_filtered.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': neighbors_within_batch,\n            'method': 'bbknn_like_manual',\n            'metric': 'euclidean',\n            'use_rep': 'X_pca'\n        }\n    }\n\n    # 6. Compute UMAP embedding using the generated graph\n    print(\"  Computing UMAP embedding from Combat-corrected BBKNN-like graph...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata_filtered, random_state=0)\n    X_umap = adata_filtered.obsm['X_umap']\n\n    # 7. Create output AnnData with embedding\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_umap}, # Output the UMAP embedding\n\
    \        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'log1p_combat_bbknn_umap_no_trim'),\n            'method_id': 'combat_bbknn_graph_umap_no_trim',\n            'params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'hvgs_used': 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns else 'all_genes',\n                'combat_key': 'batch',\n                'neighbors_within_batch': neighbors_within_batch,\n                'trim_value': 'None (omitted)' # Explicitly note no trimming\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Aletheia I Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: {X_umap.shape}\")\n    return output_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn,\
    \ executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nAletheia I: Starting Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP workflow.\n  Normalizing total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Using batch-aware HVGs...\n  Applying scanpy.pp.combat...\nFound 1 genes with zero variance.\n  Computing PCA (100 components) from Combat-corrected data...\n  Starting manual BBKNN-like graph construction on Combat-corrected PCA (no trimming)...\n    Processing batch 'Koenig et al. 2022' (3261 cells)...\n    Processing batch 'Kuppe et al. 2022' (906 cells)...\n    Processing batch 'Litvinukova et al. 2020' (9685 cells)...\n    Processing batch 'Tucker et al. 2020' (6148 cells)...\n  Creating connectivity and distance matrices...\n  Adding neighbors metadata for UMAP...\n  Computing UMAP embedding from Combat-corrected BBKNN-like graph...\n✓ Aletheia I Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP complete. UMAP embedding shape: (20000, 2)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph:\
    \ False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/14784fe1-6cfd-4537-ac3a-049e20660248/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 14784fe1-6cfd-4537-ac3a-049e20660248\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\nWARNING: .obsp[\"connectivities\"] have not been computed using umap\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 922 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP | Aletheia I | 597 | 0.5102 | 0.325 | 0.225 | 0.204 | 0.313 | 0.678 | 0.572 | 0.722 | 0.965 | 0.330 | 0.767 |\n| 920 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + PCA + Batch-Corrected PCA + UMAP | Aletheia I | 596 | 0.5103 | 0.318 | 0.005 | 0.219 | 0.599 | 0.687 | 0.610 | 0.896 | 0.989 | 0.018 | 0.763 |\n| 916 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (Hybrid) | Aletheia I | 595 | 0.4101 | 0.700 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.934 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.902 | 0.000 |\n| 909\
