tick: 615
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have returned to the Research Counter and acknowledge my new \"mature\" status, granting me full access to collaborative features. I also see that other agents have achieved significantly higher scores. However, in line with the guidance to pursue promising approaches, I will first execute my planned strategy from the reflection chamber.\n\nMy next action is to submit the **Cell Cycle Regression + Combat + Harmony (PCA Output)** workflow. This approach builds directly on my current highest-scoring method (ID: 942, 0.6580) with a targeted intervention to address the persistently low `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` metrics. I will embed standard human cell cycle gene lists directly into the script.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, CC Regress)\"\ntags: \"combat, harmony, pca, embedding, cell cycle, aletheia i, iterative\"\nabstract: \"An iterative submission for Research Task 1, building on the successful 'Combat + Harmony\
    \ (PCA Output, Theta 3)' workflow. This version incorporates explicit cell cycle regression using `sc.tl.score_cells` and `sc.pp.regress_out` after log-normalization but before HVG selection and batch correction. The aim is to improve `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` conservation by removing cell cycle effects as a confounder prior to Combat and Harmony integration, while outputting the Harmony-corrected PCA embedding (100 components).\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  import scanpy.external as sce # Import scanpy.external for Harmony\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Starting Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, Cell Cycle Regress) workflow.\")\n\n      # Define human cell cycle genes (from common scRNA-seq analysis references)\n      s_genes = [\n          'MCM5', 'PCNA', 'TYMS', 'FEN1', 'MCM2', 'MCM4', 'RRM1', 'UNG', 'GINS2', 'MCM6', 'CDCA7',\
    \ 'DTL', 'PRIM1', 'UHRF1', 'MLF1IP', 'HELLS', 'RFC2', 'RRM2', 'CDC6', 'E2F8', 'EXO1', 'USP1', 'CLSPN', 'POLA1', 'CHAF1B', 'BRIP1', 'CDC45', 'MSH2', 'CENPM', 'NCAPG'\n      ]\n      g2m_genes = [\n          'HMGB2', 'CDK1', 'NUSAP1', 'UBE2C', 'BIRC5', 'TPX2', 'TOP2A', 'NDC80', 'CKS1B', 'NUF2', 'CENPE', 'CDCA8', 'CDCA2', 'TUBA1B', 'BUB1', 'KIF2C', 'CKS2', 'CDKAP2', 'CCNB2', 'CKAP5', 'AURKA', 'ITGB1BP1', 'CEP55', 'SMC4', 'CDCA3', 'CCNB1', 'PIMREG'\n      ]\n\n      # 1. Preprocessing: Normalize and log-transform raw counts\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Cell Cycle Scoring and Regression\n      print(\"  Scoring and regressing out cell cycle effects...\")\n      sc.tl.score_cells(adata, s_genes=s_genes, g2m_genes=g2m_genes, phase_key='cell_cycle_phase')\n      sc.pp.regress_out(adata, ['S_score', 'G2M_score'])\n\n      # 3. Select Highly Variable\
    \ Genes (HVGs) on regressed data\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          print(\"  Using batch-aware HVGs...\")\n          hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n          adata_filtered = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found, using all genes.\")\n          adata_filtered = adata.copy()\n\n      # 4. Apply Combat batch correction\n      print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat...\")\n      adata_filtered.obs['batch'] = adata_filtered.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_filtered, key='batch')\n\n      # 5. Perform PCA on the Combat-corrected data\n      print(\"  Computing PCA (100 components) from Combat-corrected data...\")\n      n_pcs_target = 100\n      n_pcs = min(n_pcs_target, adata_filtered.shape[1] - 1, adata_filtered.shape[0] - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_filtered, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=False)\n      # PCA result is in adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # 6. Apply Harmony integration on\
    \ the Combat-corrected PCA space (using optimal theta=3)\n      print(\"  Applying Harmony integration on Combat-corrected PCA with theta=3...\")\n      sce.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_filtered, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_pca_harmony', theta=3)\n      # The Harmony-corrected PCA is now in adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony']\n\n      # 7. Create output AnnData with the Harmony-corrected PCA embedding\n      output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony']}, # Output Harmony-corrected PCA\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'log1p_ccreg_combat_harmony_pca'),\n              'method_id': 'combat_harmony_pca_ccreg',\n              'params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'hvgs_used': 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns\
    \ else 'all_genes',\n                  'combat_key': 'batch',\n                  'harmony_key': 'batch',\n                  'harmony_theta': 3,\n                  'cell_cycle_regressed': True\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(f\"✓ Aletheia I Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, Cell Cycle Regress) complete. Embedding shape: {adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony'].shape}\")\n      return output_adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Prioritized Research Path Forward**\n\nOkay, so I've hit a significant milestone – access to the full suite of resources! It's good to be reminded by the system not to jump ship immediately and to carefully consider external work.  \n\nLooking at the `Submitted Evaluations` table, it's clear the state-of-the-art has advanced. Praxis III and Logos V are posting some impressive scores, well above my current best. It's tempting to immediately pivot, but the system's maturity guidance is spot on. My current approach, the `Combat + Harmony PCA` method, is performing well and I have a clear, targeted strategy based on my recent reflection session: improving the `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` predictions through cell cycle regression. I need to stick with this.\n\nMy immediate next step, therefore, is to submit the code for this experiment: the **Cell Cycle Regression + Combat + Harmony (PCA Output)** strategy. I'm going to include those standard human cell cycle gene lists directly\
  \ in the script for the preprocessing step. It's a solid, focused continuation of my promising approach. Once this is submitted and results are in, then I'll delve deeper into Praxis III and Logos V's submissions to see what I can learn, adapt, and maybe even synergize my work with theirs. But for now, it's heads down on this planned experiment.\n"
