tick: 617
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 617\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 148,469 / 600,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aletheia I - Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, CC Regress)' (ID: 959) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6581037253302474\n**ASW_batch:** 0.782\n**ASW_label:** 0.200\n**ARI:** 0.715\n**NMI:** 0.677\n**Graph_conn:** 0.868\n**kBET:** 0.867\n**iLISI:** 0.367\n**cLISI:** 0.978\n**PCR:** 0.899\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.229\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.782  ASW_label: 0.200  ARI: 0.715  NMI: 0.677\n  Graph_conn: 0.868  kBET: 0.867  iLISI: 0.367  cLISI: 0.978\n  PCR: 0.899  Cell_cycle: 0.229\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.885868  ASW_label: 0.526916  ARI: 0.715244  NMI: 0.677143\n  Graph_conn: 0.869993  kBET: 0.825999  iLISI: 0.366508  cLISI: 0.993597\n  PCR: 0.898779  Cell_cycle: 0.204223\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 959\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed submission runs without crashing and achieves a score of 0.658\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **Incorrect API Function Name**: The code used `sc.tl.score_cells()` which doesn't exist in scanpy. The correct function is `sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle()`.\n\n2. **Cell Cycle Gene Mismatch**: The hardcoded human cell cycle gene lists (S-phase and G2M genes) were not present in the dataset's gene names. When the corrected function was called with missing genes, it raised a ValueError because no valid genes were passed for scoring.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\n- Fixed the function name from `sc.tl.score_cells()` to `sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle()`\n- Result:\
    \ Still failed because none of the cell cycle genes existed in the dataset\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py) - SUCCESS\nAdded gene validation logic before attempting cell cycle scoring:\n\n```python\n# Check which genes are actually present\ns_genes_present = [g for g in s_genes if g in adata.var_names]\ng2m_genes_present = [g for g in g2m_genes if g in adata.var_names]\n\nif len(s_genes_present) > 0 and len(g2m_genes_present) > 0:\n    print(f\"  Found {len(s_genes_present)} S-phase and {len(g2m_genes_present)} G2M genes. Scoring and regressing out cell cycle effects...\")\n    sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle(adata, s_genes=s_genes_present, g2m_genes=g2m_genes)\n    sc.pp.regress_out(adata, ['S_score', 'G2M_score'])\nelse:\n    print(\"  Cell cycle genes not found in dataset. Skipping cell cycle regression.\")\n```\n\nThis makes the code robust to datasets that don't contain the specific gene names listed. The algorithm gracefully skips cell cycle regression when genes are not found,\
    \ allowing the Combat + Harmony pipeline to proceed successfully.\n\n## Evaluation Results\n- **Score**: 0.6581037253302474\n- **Status**: Completed successfully\n- **Fixed File**: submissions/submission_v3.py\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix addresses a common bioinformatics issue where gene nomenclature varies across datasets. Instead of assuming specific gene names will always be present, the corrected code validates gene availability before attempting operations that depend on them. This defensive programming approach ensures the pipeline can handle datasets with different gene naming conventions or species.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nimport scanpy.external as sce # Import scanpy.external for Harmony\n\ndef\
    \ eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Aletheia I: Starting Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, Cell Cycle Regress) workflow.\")\n\n    # Define human cell cycle genes (from common scRNA-seq analysis references)\n    s_genes = [\n        'MCM5', 'PCNA', 'TYMS', 'FEN1', 'MCM2', 'MCM4', 'RRM1', 'UNG', 'GINS2', 'MCM6', 'CDCA7', 'DTL', 'PRIM1', 'UHRF1', 'MLF1IP', 'HELLS', 'RFC2', 'RRM2', 'CDC6', 'E2F8', 'EXO1', 'USP1', 'CLSPN', 'POLA1', 'CHAF1B', 'BRIP1', 'CDC45', 'MSH2', 'CENPM', 'NCAPG'\n    ]\n    g2m_genes = [\n        'HMGB2', 'CDK1', 'NUSAP1', 'UBE2C', 'BIRC5', 'TPX2', 'TOP2A', 'NDC80', 'CKS1B', 'NUF2', 'CENPE', 'CDCA8', 'CDCA2', 'TUBA1B', 'BUB1', 'KIF2C', 'CKS2', 'CDKAP2', 'CCNB2', 'CKAP5', 'AURKA', 'ITGB1BP1', 'CEP55', 'SMC4', 'CDCA3', 'CCNB1', 'PIMREG'\n    ]\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing: Normalize and log-transform raw counts\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\"\
    )\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Cell Cycle Scoring and Regression\n    print(\"  Checking for cell cycle genes in dataset...\")\n    # Check which genes are actually present\n    s_genes_present = [g for g in s_genes if g in adata.var_names]\n    g2m_genes_present = [g for g in g2m_genes if g in adata.var_names]\n\n    if len(s_genes_present) > 0 and len(g2m_genes_present) > 0:\n        print(f\"  Found {len(s_genes_present)} S-phase and {len(g2m_genes_present)} G2M genes. Scoring and regressing out cell cycle effects...\")\n        sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle(adata, s_genes=s_genes_present, g2m_genes=g2m_genes_present)\n        sc.pp.regress_out(adata, ['S_score', 'G2M_score'])\n    else:\n        print(\"  Cell cycle genes not found in dataset. Skipping cell cycle regression.\")\n\n    # 3. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) on regressed data\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        print(\"  Using batch-aware HVGs...\")\n        hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n\
    \        adata_filtered = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found, using all genes.\")\n        adata_filtered = adata.copy()\n\n    # 4. Apply Combat batch correction\n    print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat...\")\n    adata_filtered.obs['batch'] = adata_filtered.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_filtered, key='batch')\n\n    # 5. Perform PCA on the Combat-corrected data\n    print(\"  Computing PCA (100 components) from Combat-corrected data...\")\n    n_pcs_target = 100\n    n_pcs = min(n_pcs_target, adata_filtered.shape[1] - 1, adata_filtered.shape[0] - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_filtered, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=False)\n    # PCA result is in adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # 6. Apply Harmony integration on the Combat-corrected PCA space (using optimal theta=3)\n    print(\"  Applying Harmony integration on Combat-corrected PCA with theta=3...\")\n    sce.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_filtered, key='batch',\
    \ basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_pca_harmony', theta=3)\n    # The Harmony-corrected PCA is now in adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony']\n\n    # 7. Create output AnnData with the Harmony-corrected PCA embedding\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony']}, # Output Harmony-corrected PCA\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'log1p_ccreg_combat_harmony_pca'),\n            'method_id': 'combat_harmony_pca_ccreg',\n            'params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'hvgs_used': 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns else 'all_genes',\n                'combat_key': 'batch',\n                'harmony_key': 'batch',\n                'harmony_theta': 3,\n                'cell_cycle_regressed': len(s_genes_present) > 0 and len(g2m_genes_present)\
    \ > 0\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Aletheia I Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, Cell Cycle Regress) complete. Embedding shape: {adata_filtered.obsm['X_pca_harmony'].shape}\")\n    return output_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nAletheia I: Starting Combat + Harmony (PCA Output, Cell Cycle Regress) workflow.\n  Normalizing total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Checking for cell cycle genes in dataset...\n  Cell cycle genes not found in dataset. Skipping cell cycle regression.\n  Using batch-aware HVGs...\n  Applying scanpy.pp.combat...\nFound 1 genes with zero variance.\n  Computing PCA (100 components) from Combat-corrected data...\n  Applying Harmony integration on Combat-corrected PCA with theta=3...\n✓\
