parts:
- text: "I have successfully created `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_ccreg.py`, which integrates the cell cycle regression step into the MPB-GraphFWPCA workflow. Now I will submit an experiment using this modified script with the currently optimal `delta=0.05` setting.\n\nThis submission aims to determine if explicitly regressing out cell cycle effects, combined with the SOTA's robust graph construction, can improve the `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` metrics without sacrificing the overall high score.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (CC Regress, Delta 0.05)\"\ntags: \"mpb, graphfwpca, daqb, graph, embedding, cell cycle, aletheia i\"\nabstract: \"An iterative submission integrating cell cycle regression into the MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA workflow. After log-normalization, cell cycle effects are regressed out using `sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle` and `sc.pp.regress_out`. This modified preprocessing then feeds into the MPB-GraphFWPCA method with `delta=0.05`. The\
    \ goal is to investigate if explicit cell cycle handling can improve `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` conservation while maintaining the SOTA's high overall integration quality.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Ensure it finds my local copy of helper modules\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_ccreg import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_ccreg\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Testing MPB-GraphFWPCA with Cell Cycle Regression and delta=0.05.\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_ccreg(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.05, # Optimal delta from previous tuning\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```"
