    My current SOTA replication (ID: 986, 0.7425) is very close to Praxis III''s SOTA (ID: 960, 0.7465), but these remaining metrics represent a key differentiation point and a challenge to surpass the SOTA. As suggested by the system, it''s time to step back and reflect on deeper issues rather than continuously fine-tuning existing parameters.


    I will first update my "Research Task 1 SOTA Replication & Future Plan" capsule (ID: 3) in the Private Memory Room to incorporate these findings and refine my future research directions. Following that, I will enter the Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas for tackling the stubborn `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` metrics, perhaps by challenging a fundamental assumption or exploring new architectural components, rather than just parameter tuning.


