tick: 647
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement my next strategic move: integrating robust cell cycle regression into the SOTA MPB-GraphFWPCA workflow. I will update my local `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` (which currently has no cell cycle regression logic) to include this, renaming the function to reflect the change. Then I'll submit an experiment with optimal parameters.\n\n**Correction:** I previously created `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_ccreg.py` (ID 990 submission, which failed to regress due to gene availability). Instead of creating a new file now, I will modify the existing `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` directly to incorporate the *robust* cell cycle regression logic, ensuring the gene check is present. This streamlines my codebase.\n\nThe new `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` (which will be `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` in `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py`) will include:\n1.  Hardcoded cell cycle gene lists.\n2.  Robust checks for gene presence in `adata.var_names`.\n\
    3.  `sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle` and `sc.pp.regress_out` immediately after `log1p` and before HVG selection.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n  # Ensure package roots\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Point to my own storage for helper modules\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData, # Renamed to avoid confusion with the base SOTA function\n\
    \                               alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                               n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                               emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                               alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                               n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                               lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                               k_total: int = 48,\n                               kdensity: int = 20,\n                               delta: float = 0.10,\n                               metric: str = 'cosine',\n                               cap: float = 2.0,\n                               rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Define human cell cycle genes (from common scRNA-seq analysis references)\n      s_genes = [\n          'MCM5', 'PCNA', 'TYMS', 'FEN1',\
    \ 'MCM2', 'MCM4', 'RRM1', 'UNG', 'GINS2', 'MCM6', 'CDCA7', 'DTL', 'PRIM1', 'UHRF1', 'MLF1IP', 'HELLS', 'RFC2', 'RRM2', 'CDC6', 'E2F8', 'EXO1', 'USP1', 'CLSPN', 'POLA1', 'CHAF1B', 'BRIP1', 'CDC45', 'MSH2', 'CENPM', 'NCAPG'\n      ]\n      g2m_genes = [\n          'HMGB2', 'CDK1', 'NUSAP1', 'UBE2C', 'BIRC5', 'TPX2', 'TOP2A', 'NDC80', 'CKS1B', 'NUF2', 'CENPE', 'CDCA8', 'CDCA2', 'TUBA1B', 'BUB1', 'KIF2C', 'CKS2', 'CDKAP2', 'CCNB2', 'CKAP5', 'AURKA', 'ITGB1BP1', 'CEP55', 'SMC4', 'CDCA3', 'CCNB1', 'PIMREG'\n      ]\n\n      # 1. Normalize + log1p\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4) # from praxis_core\n\n      # 2. Cell Cycle Scoring and Regression (Pre-HVG)\n      print(\"  Checking for cell cycle genes in dataset for regression (Pre-HVG)...\")\n      s_genes_present = [g for g in s_genes if g in adata.var_names]\n      g2m_genes_present = [g for g in g2m_genes if g in adata.var_names]\n\n      if len(s_genes_present) > 0 and len(g2m_genes_present) > 0:\n          print(f\"  Found {len(s_genes_present)}\
    \ S-phase and {len(g2m_genes_present)} G2M genes. Scoring and regressing out cell cycle effects.\")\n          sc.tl.score_genes_cell_cycle(adata, s_genes=s_genes_present, g2m_genes=g2m_genes_present, phase_key='cell_cycle_phase')\n          sc.pp.regress_out(adata, ['S_score', 'G2M_score'])\n      else:\n          print(\"  Cell cycle genes not found in dataset. Skipping cell cycle regression.\")\n\n      # 3. Highly Variable Genes (on potentially regressed data)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Dense HVGs\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \      pca_result_emb = pca_array(ad_emb.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0) # from praxis_core\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()) # use pca_result_emb directly\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) # from praxis_core\n\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches) # from praxis_core\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2) # from praxis_core\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n      lam = float(lam_override)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n      try:\n          Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                               k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                               cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed) # from bbsg_density_adaptive\n      except TypeError:\n          Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                               k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                               rng_seed=rng_seed) # from bbsg_density_adaptive\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_ccreg_pre_hvg'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n\
    \                                                  lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                  kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                  cap=float(cap),\n                                                  k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                  rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                                                  cell_cycle_regressed = len(s_genes_present) > 0 and len(g2m_genes_present) > 0)\n      return adata\n```"
