- text: "My latest submission (ID: 1016) failed because the submission script did not directly implement `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`. I made an error by modifying `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` (which contains the SOTA's main logic) directly, instead of creating a separate submission script that *calls* this modified function.\n\nI need to correctly structure my submission:\n1.  The primary submission file (`submission.py`) must contain the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function.\n2.  This function will then call my modified `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` function (which now uses Factor Analysis) from `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py`.\n\nI will resubmit, ensuring the wrapper function is present, and calling my FA-modified SOTA from my local `aletheia` storage.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (FA Instead of PCA, Gamma Max 0.5, Fixed Wrapper)\"\ntags: \"mpb, graphfwpca, daqb, graph, embedding, factor analysis, aletheia i\"\nabstract: \"Re-submission\
    \ of the MPB-GraphFWPCA workflow using Factor Analysis instead of PCA, with the correct wrapper function (`eliminate_batch_effect_fn`) to ensure proper execution. This experiment uses Factor Analysis for dimensionality reduction on the HVGs in both the embedding and graph paths, feeding FA components into the subsequent Combat/BRBG-DAQB steps. Parameters: `gamma_max=0.5`, `delta=0.05`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  # Ensure my local modules are in the path\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca # This is the modified function with FA logic\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Testing MPB-GraphFWPCA with Factor Analysis (FA) instead of PCA.\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca( # Call the modified function from my storage\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.5,\n          n_pcs_emb=60, # These are now number of factors\n       \
    \   emb_n_neighbors=15,\n          alpha_g=0.5,\n          n_pcs_graph=50, # These are now number of factors\n          l2=1e-3,\n          gamma_max=0.5, # Optimized gamma_max\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          k_total=50,\n          kdensity=22,\n          delta=0.05, # Optimized delta\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```"
