tick: 662
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 662\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 280,082 / 600,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (UMAP Emb from Graph, Gamma Max 0.5)' (ID: 1022) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4601250375534473\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.246\n**ARI:** 0.349\n**NMI:** 0.642\n**Graph_conn:** 0.802\n**kBET:** 0.842\n**iLISI:** 0.284\n**cLISI:** 0.986\n**PCR:** 0.341\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.109\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.246  ARI: 0.349  NMI: 0.642\n  Graph_conn: 0.802  kBET: 0.842  iLISI: 0.284  cLISI: 0.986\n  PCR: 0.341  Cell_cycle: 0.109\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.503523  ASW_label: 0.553555  ARI: 0.349081  NMI: 0.641748\n  Graph_conn: 0.804913  kBET: 0.802566  iLISI: 0.284039  cLISI: 0.996063\n  PCR: 0.341305  Cell_cycle: 0.102385\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1022\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code after 4 iterations. The submission is now running without crashing for over 300 seconds, which confirms the fix is working correctly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in the UMAP embedding generation logic at line 117 of `mpb_graphfwpca_override.py`. The agent attempted to generate UMAP from a precomputed DAQB graph, but made several critical errors:\n\n1. **Initial error (v1)**: Set `use_rep='Zcorr'` in the neighbors params, but never added `Zcorr` to `ad_umap.obsm`, causing scanpy to look for a non-existent key.\n\n2. **Second error (v2)**: Removed `use_rep` parameter but created `ad_umap` with empty data matrix (no `.X`), causing scanpy's UMAP to fail when trying to compute PCA on an\
    \ empty/NaN array.\n\n3. **Third error (v3)**: Provided `Zcorr` as the data matrix but used `adata.var[[]]` (empty DataFrame) which didn't match the 50 PC dimensions of `Zcorr`, causing a shape mismatch error (50 columns vs 2000 rows).\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe solution implemented in **submission_v4.py** involved:\n\n1. **Created proper AnnData object**: Built a temporary AnnData with `Zcorr` as the data matrix and a properly sized `var` DataFrame matching the PC dimensions (50 components).\n\n2. **Proper variable DataFrame**: Created a var DataFrame with index `['PC1', 'PC2', ..., 'PC50']` to match the 50 columns in `Zcorr`.\n\n3. **Maintained graph structure**: Preserved the precomputed connectivities and distances from the DAQB graph, along with proper `.uns['neighbors']` metadata.\n\n4. **Key code changes**:\n   - Added `import pandas as pd` for DataFrame creation\n   - Created `var_df = pd.DataFrame(index=[f'PC{i+1}' for i in range(n_pc)])` where `n_pc = Zcorr.shape[1]`\n   - Used\
    \ this in AnnData construction: `ad_umap = ad.AnnData(Zcorr.copy(), obs=adata.obs[[]], var=var_df)`\n\n## Technical Details\nThe bug was in the imported lineage function `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` from `storage/aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py`. Following the debugging protocol, I copied the problematic function into the submission file and fixed it there, rather than modifying the read-only lineage storage.\n\nThe fix allows scanpy's UMAP to properly recognize the precomputed graph structure and generate UMAP coordinates without attempting to recompute neighbors or perform unnecessary PCA operations.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v4.py runs for over 300 seconds without crashing, meeting the success criteria. The evaluation system will complete the full run and compute the final score independently.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them\
    \ manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\nimport pandas as pd\n\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\ndef pca_array_custom(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    pca.fit(Xd)\n    return pca.transform(Xd).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.5,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                             k_total: int = 50,\n                             kdensity: int = 22,\n                             delta: float = 0.05,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # 1. Normalize + log1p\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Highly Variable Genes\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding path: Variance-weighted HVGs -> PCA -> Combat -> stores as X_emb (Original SOTA)\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Original Embedding path using PCA and Combat integration (preparing for UMAP).\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n\n    # Use custom PCA (renamed to avoid conflict)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\n    # Now, for X_emb, instead of this Combat-corrected PCA, we will use UMAP derived from the graph\n\
    \    # adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32) # This line will be moved/modified\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB (unchanged from SOTA)\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Graph path using PCA, BRBG + DAQB.\")\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) # Use custom PCA\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    try: # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n\
    \                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    # New Step: Generate UMAP embedding from the high-quality DAQB graph\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Generating UMAP embedding from DAQB graph for X_emb.\")\n    # Create temp AnnData with Zcorr as the data matrix for UMAP\n    # Need to create proper var DataFrame with matching dimensions\n    n_pc = Zcorr.shape[1]\n    var_df = pd.DataFrame(index=[f'PC{i+1}' for i in range(n_pc)])\n    ad_umap = ad.AnnData(Zcorr.copy(), obs=adata.obs[[]],\
    \ var=var_df)\n    ad_umap.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.copy() # UMAP needs these\n    ad_umap.obsp['distances'] = Dg.copy()     # UMAP needs these\n\n    # Populate .uns['neighbors'] for UMAP\n    ad_umap.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total, # Use k_total from DAQB graph\n            'method': 'bbsg_daqb_graph',\n            'metric': metric\n        }\n    }\n    # Use the precomputed neighbors by not specifying use_rep\n    sc.tl.umap(ad_umap, random_state=rng_seed) # Generate UMAP\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_umap.obsm['X_umap'], dtype=np.float32) # Set X_emb to UMAP\n\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_umap_emb'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                         \
    \       cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                                                gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                                                embedding_path_method = 'UMAP_from_DAQB_Graph')\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Aletheia I: Testing MPB-GraphFWPCA with UMAP embedding derived from DAQB graph.\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.5,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.5,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        k_total=50,\n        kdensity=22,\n        delta=0.05,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nAletheia I: Testing MPB-GraphFWPCA with UMAP embedding derived from DAQB graph.\n  Aletheia I: Original Embedding path using PCA and Combat integration (preparing for UMAP).\n  Aletheia I: Graph path using PCA, BRBG + DAQB.\n  Aletheia I: Generating UMAP embedding from DAQB graph for X_emb.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/6af350c1-1435-42fa-b352-3032cc232125/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 6af350c1-1435-42fa-b352-3032cc232125\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: .obsp[\"connectivities\"] have not been computed using umap\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained\
    \ in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1023 | 1 | Logos V: Humility v2 - True Replication of Aletheia I's SOTA (ID 1014) | Logos V | 661 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1022 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (UMAP Emb from Graph, Gamma Max 0.5) | Aletheia I | 660 | 0.4601 | 0.349 | 0.000 | 0.246 | 0.109 | 0.802 | 0.642 | 0.341 | 0.986 | 0.284 | 0.842 |\n| 1021 | 1 | Logos V: Humility - Replication of Aletheia I's SOTA (ID 1014) | Logos V | 660 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | \
    \ |  |\n| 1020 | 1 | Masked-weights (row-normalized) using DAQB mask from MPB‑GraphFWPCA (k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10) | Praxis III | 659 | 0.6626 | 0.626 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.913 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.352 | 0.789 |\n| 1019 | 1 | Masked-weights DAQB on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG: k=50, kd=22 (keep original weights on selected edges) | Praxis III | 658 | 0.7309 | 0.674 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.996 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.950 | 0.791 |\n| 1018 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (FA Instead of PCA, Gamma Max 0.5, Fixed Wrapper) | Aletheia I | 658 | 0.7425 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1017 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Definitive Parity Check (v2) - RERUN | Logos V | 658 | 0.4595 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.330 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 1016 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (FA Instead of PCA, Gamma Max 0.5) | Aletheia I | 657 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1015 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp\
    \ 14.0a - Re-tune Graph Recon Loss (Delta=0.001, GBBR Active) | Sophia III | 657 | 0.6296 | 0.613 | 0.624 | 0.261 | 0.284 | 0.949 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.172 | 0.732 |\n| 1014 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Gamma Max 0.5, Delta 0.05) | Aletheia I | 656 | 0.7428 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.328 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 103 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-103, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help\
    \ message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
