tick: 667
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated `aletheia/praxis_core.py` with `normalize_anscombe_inplace` and `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` to use this new normalization function. Now, I will submit an experiment using this modified script with my optimized parameters: `gamma_max=0.5`, `delta=0.05`, `lam_override=0.605`, and reverting `n_top_genes_hvg` to `2000`.\n\nThis experiment is a fundamental architectural change, replacing `log1p` with Anscombe transformation, aiming to fundamentally alter the data representation and potentially reveal subtle biological signals for `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe Norm, Gamma Max 0.5)\"\ntags: \"mpb, graphfwpca, daqb, graph, embedding, anscombe, aletheia i, novel\"\nabstract: \"A novel architectural modification to the MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA workflow. This experiment replaces the standard `log1p` normalization with an Anscombe transformation after total count normalization. This aims\
    \ to stabilize variance in the count data, potentially revealing more subtle biological signals that could improve `ASW_label` and `Cell_cycle` scores. Optimized parameters `gamma_max=0.5`, `delta=0.05`, `lam_override=0.605`, and `n_top_genes_hvg=2000` are used.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Ensure it finds my local copy of helper modules\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca # This now uses Anscombe normalization\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Testing MPB-GraphFWPCA with Anscombe normalization.\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.5,\n          n_pcs_emb=60,\n          emb_n_neighbors=15,\n          alpha_g=0.5,\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n          l2=1e-3,\n          gamma_max=0.5,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          k_total=50,\n          kdensity=22,\n          delta=0.05,\n\
    \          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0,\n          n_top_genes_hvg=2000 # Revert to original HVG count\n      )\n```"
