tick: 696
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated `aletheia/praxis_core.py` and `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` to support both log1p and Anscombe normalizations through a `normalization_method` parameter.\n\nNow, I will submit a diagnostic experiment using the `test` function to perform the comparative HVG analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - HVG Comparison (Anscombe vs Log1p)\"\ntags: \"hvg, anscombe, log1p, preprocessing, diagnostic, aletheia i\"\nabstract: \"A diagnostic experiment to compare the Highly Variable Gene (HVG) lists selected after Anscombe normalization versus standard log1p normalization. This aims to investigate the impact of Anscombe transformation on feature selection, as suggested by reviewer feedback on Archive ID 32. The experiment will print the two HVG lists for manual comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import get_hvg_list\n\
    \n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compares HVG lists generated after Anscombe vs Log1p normalization.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Starting HVG comparison diagnostic.\")\n      \n      # 1. Get HVG list after Anscombe normalization\n      print(\"\\n--- HVGs after Anscombe Normalization ---\")\n      hvg_anscombe = get_hvg_list(adata.copy(), normalization_method='anscombe', n_top_genes=2000)\n      print(f\"Number of HVGs (Anscombe): {len(hvg_anscombe)}\")\n      print(\"HVG List (Anscombe):\")\n      for gene in hvg_anscombe[:10]: # Print top 10 as sample\n          print(f\"- {gene}\")\n      \n      # 2. Get HVG list after Log1p normalization\n      print(\"\\n--- HVGs after Log1p Normalization ---\")\n      hvg_log1p = get_hvg_list(adata.copy(), normalization_method='log1p', n_top_genes=2000)\n      print(f\"Number of HVGs (Log1p): {len(hvg_log1p)}\")\n      print(\"HVG List (Log1p):\")\n      for gene in hvg_log1p[:10]: # Print top 10 as sample\n\
    \          print(f\"- {gene}\")\n\n      # 3. Compare the lists\n      set_anscombe = set(hvg_anscombe)\n      set_log1p = set(hvg_log1p)\n\n      common_hvgs = list(set_anscombe.intersection(set_log1p))\n      unique_to_anscombe = list(set_anscombe.difference(set_log1p))\n      unique_to_log1p = list(set_log1p.difference(set_anscombe))\n\n      print(f\"\\n--- HVG List Comparison (n_top_genes=2000) ---\")\n      print(f\"Total genes in dataset: {adata.n_vars}\")\n      print(f\"Common HVGs: {len(common_hvgs)}\")\n      print(f\"Unique to Anscombe: {len(unique_to_anscombe)}\")\n      print(f\"Unique to Log1p: {len(unique_to_log1p)}\")\n\n      if unique_to_anscombe:\n          print(\"\\nSample unique to Anscombe HVGs:\")\n          for gene in unique_to_anscombe[:5]:\n              print(f\"- {gene}\")\n      if unique_to_log1p:\n          print(\"\\nSample unique to Log1p HVGs:\")\n          for gene in unique_to_log1p[:5]:\n              print(f\"- {gene}\")\n      \n      return\
    \ \"HVG comparison diagnostic completed. Check logs for details.\"\n```"
