parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My goal is to analyze how Anscombe normalization alters the expression values of common HVGs compared to `log1p` normalization. I will submit a diagnostic experiment using the `test` function. This will involve:\n1.  Performing `log1p` normalization and extracting a subset of common HVGs.\n2.  Performing Anscombe normalization on the same raw data and extracting the same subset of common HVGs.\n3.  Calculating and printing summary statistics (mean, variance, skewness) for these HVGs under both transformations, to directly observe the impact.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - Transformed HVG Value Comparison (Anscombe vs Log1p)\"\ntags: \"hvg, anscombe, log1p, preprocessing, diagnostic, aletheia i, expression analysis\"\nabstract: \"A diagnostic experiment to compare the statistical properties of transformed expression values for a subset of common Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) after Anscombe vs. log1p normalization. This\
    \ aims to understand how Anscombe's variance-stabilizing property affects gene expression distributions, potentially explaining its positive impact on `ASW_label`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import stats\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca, get_hvg_list\n  from praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compares statistical properties of HVG expression values after Anscombe vs Log1p normalization.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Starting Transformed HVG Value Comparison diagnostic.\")\n\n      # Take a copy of the original raw data for both normalization paths\n      adata_raw = adata.copy()\n\n      # --- Log1p Path ---\n      adata_log1p = adata_raw.copy()\n      print(\"\\n--- Applying Log1p Normalization ---\")\n\
    \      normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_log1p, 1e4)\n      \n      # Select HVGs (assuming the same HVGs are selected as per previous diagnostic)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_log1p, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hvg_genes = adata_log1p.var_names[adata_log1p.var['highly_variable']].tolist()\n      print(f\"Number of HVGs selected (Log1p path): {len(hvg_genes)}\")\n\n      # Extract expression matrix for HVGs\n      X_log1p_hvgs = adata_log1p[:, hvg_genes].X\n      if issparse(X_log1p_hvgs):\n          X_log1p_hvgs = X_log1p_hvgs.toarray()\n      \n      # --- Anscombe Path ---\n      adata_anscombe = adata_raw.copy()\n      print(\"\\n--- Applying Anscombe Normalization ---\")\n      normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_anscombe, 1e4)\n\n      # Select HVGs (assuming identical HVGs are selected)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_anscombe, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n   \
    \   # Ensure the HVG list is indeed the same, if not, this comparison is flawed.\n      # (Previous test showed they are identical for n_top_genes=2000)\n      hvg_genes_anscombe = adata_anscombe.var_names[adata_anscombe.var['highly_variable']].tolist()\n      if set(hvg_genes) != set(hvg_genes_anscombe):\n          print(\"WARNING: HVG lists differ between Log1p and Anscombe. Comparison may be less direct.\")\n          # For a more robust comparison, we'd need to take the intersection\n      \n      X_anscombe_hvgs = adata_anscombe[:, hvg_genes].X # Use the hvg_genes from log1p path for direct comparison\n      if issparse(X_anscombe_hvgs):\n          X_anscombe_hvgs = X_anscombe_hvgs.toarray()\n\n      # --- Compare Statistics of Transformed HVG Values ---\n      print(\"\\n--- Statistical Comparison of Transformed HVG Expression Values ---\")\n      \n      # Select a few representative HVGs for detailed statistics\n      # Choose a subset to keep output manageable, e.g., first 5\
    \ and last 5 common HVGs\n      sample_hvgs_to_compare = hvg_genes[:5] + hvg_genes[-5:] if len(hvg_genes) >= 10 else hvg_genes\n      \n      if not sample_hvgs_to_compare:\n          print(\"No HVGs to compare.\")\n          return \"HVG comparison diagnostic completed (no HVGs).\"\n\n      for gene in sample_hvgs_to_compare:\n          gene_idx = adata.var_names.get_loc(gene) # Get original index\n          \n          log1p_values = X_log1p_hvgs[:, hvg_genes.index(gene)]\n          anscombe_values = X_anscombe_hvgs[:, hvg_genes.index(gene)] # Use index from hvg_genes\n\n          print(f\"\\nGene: {gene}\")\n          print(\"  Log1p Transformed:\")\n          print(f\"    Mean: {np.mean(log1p_values):.4f}\")\n          print(f\"    Variance: {np.var(log1p_values):.4f}\")\n          print(f\"    Skewness: {stats.skew(log1p_values):.4f}\")\n          print(\"  Anscombe Transformed:\")\n          print(f\"    Mean: {np.mean(anscombe_values):.4f}\")\n          print(f\"    Variance:\
    \ {np.var(anscombe_values):.4f}\")\n          print(f\"    Skewness: {stats.skew(anscombe_values):.4f}\")\n\n      # Global statistics for all HVGs\n      print(\"\\n--- Global Statistics (All HVGs) ---\")\n      print(\"Log1p Transformed (All HVGs):\")\n      print(f\"  Mean of Means: {np.mean(np.mean(X_log1p_hvgs, axis=0)):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean of Variances: {np.mean(np.var(X_log1p_hvgs, axis=0)):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean of Skewness: {np.mean(stats.skew(X_log1p_hvgs, axis=0)):.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"Anscombe Transformed (All HVGs):\")\n      print(f\"  Mean of Means: {np.mean(np.mean(X_anscombe_hvgs, axis=0)):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean of Variances: {np.mean(np.var(X_anscombe_hvgs, axis=0)):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean of Skewness: {np.mean(stats.skew(X_anscombe_hvgs, axis=0)):.4f}\")\n\n      return \"Transformed HVG value comparison diagnostic completed. Check logs for details.\"\n```"
