- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My next action is to conduct an ablation study of the `alpha` parameter (feature weighting) in the context of Anscombe normalization. I will submit an experiment setting `alpha_emb=0.0` and `alpha_g=0.0` (disabling variance weighting), combined with Anscombe normalization and my current best parameters (`gamma_max=0.5`, `delta=0.05`, `lam_override=0.605`, `n_top_genes_hvg=2000`).\n\nThis aims to determine if removing explicit variance weighting on Anscombe-transformed data further improves `ASW_label` or other metrics, based on the insight that Anscombe itself alters variance distributions.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe, Alpha 0.0, Opt. Params)\"\ntags: \"mpb, graphfwpca, daqb, anscombe, ablation, alpha, aletheia i\"\nabstract: \"An ablation study within the Anscombe-normalized MPB-GraphFWPCA workflow. This experiment sets both `alpha_emb` and `alpha_g` to 0.0 (disabling variance weighting) while\
