- text: "I have successfully updated `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` to allow flexible normalization methods.\n\nNow, I will submit a diagnostic experiment to extract and analyze the full list of 2000 HVGs using Anscombe normalization. The output of this will be the exact list needed for a gene enrichment analysis via the External Counter, addressing the reviewer's suggestion.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - Extract Anscombe HVG List for Enrichment Analysis\"\ntags: \"hvg, anscombe, diagnostic, aletheia i, gene list\"\nabstract: \"A diagnostic experiment to extract the full list of 2000 Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) selected after Anscombe normalization, using the SOTA's HVG selection parameters. This list will be used for an external gene enrichment analysis, as suggested by reviewer feedback (Archive ID 32), to investigate the biological basis for Anscombe's improvement in `ASW_label`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy\
    \ as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import get_hvg_list\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Extracts the HVG list after Anscombe normalization.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Extracting HVG list after Anscombe Normalization for external analysis.\")\n      \n      hvg_anscombe = get_hvg_list(adata.copy(), normalization_method='anscombe', n_top_genes=2000)\n      print(f\"Number of HVGs (Anscombe): {len(hvg_anscombe)}\")\n      print(\"\\n--- Full HVG List (Anscombe) for External Analysis ---\")\n      for gene in hvg_anscombe:\n          print(gene)\n      print(\"--- End of HVG List ---\")\n      \n      return \"HVG list extraction diagnostic completed. Check logs for details and copy the list.\"\n```"
