parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My next action is to conduct an ablation study of the `alpha` parameter (feature weighting) in the context of Anscombe normalization. I will submit an experiment setting `alpha_emb=0.0` and `alpha_g=0.0` (disabling variance weighting), combined with Anscombe normalization and my current best parameters (`gamma_max=0.5`, `delta=0.05`, `lam_override=0.605`, `n_top_genes_hvg=2000`).\n\nThis aims to determine if eliminating explicit variance weighting on Anscombe-transformed data further improves `ASW_label` or other metrics by leveraging Anscombe's inherent variance-stabilizing properties, while also considering the output from my previous diagnostic that showed Anscombe increases overall variance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe, Alpha 0.0, Opt. Params) - Resubmit\"\ntags: \"mpb, graphfwpca, daqb, anscombe, ablation, alpha, aletheia i\"\nabstract: \"Re-submission of an ablation study within the Anscombe-normalized\
    \ MPB-GraphFWPCA workflow. This experiment sets both `alpha_emb` and `alpha_g` to 0.0 (disabling variance weighting) while utilizing Anscombe normalization and optimized MPB-GraphFWPCA parameters. The goal is to re-confirm if eliminating explicit variance weighting on Anscombe-transformed data further improves `ASW_label` or other metrics by leveraging Anscombe's inherent variance-stabilizing properties.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Aletheia I: Testing MPB-GraphFWPCA with Anscombe norm, Alpha 0.0 (Resubmit).\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.0, # Modified: Disable variance weighting\n          n_pcs_emb=60,\n          emb_n_neighbors=15,\n          alpha_g=0.0,   # Modified: Disable variance weighting\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n\
    \          l2=1e-3,\n          gamma_max=0.5,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          k_total=50,\n          kdensity=22,\n          delta=0.05,\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0,\n          n_top_genes_hvg=2000,\n          normalization_method='anscombe' # Explicitly use Anscombe\n      )\n```"
