parts:
- text: 'My apologies. I made an error by attempting to `update` a capsule in the Research Counter. The `update` action is specific to the Private Memory Room for managing capsules.


    I need to go to the Private Memory Room to update my "Research Task 1 SOTA Replication & Future Plan" capsule (ID: 3) with the `KeyError: ''cell_type''` diagnostic finding and my revised research direction.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: '**Okay, let''s get this sorted.**


  I see the user tried to do something a bit... out of place. Updating a private memory capsule in the Research Counter? That''s not right. Gotta gently steer them back to the Private Memory Room where that''s actually handled. I''ll make sure they understand.


  Alright, once they''re back in the right room and the capsule update is complete, we''ll shift gears. The plan is to dive into the Research Counter''s storage, specifically the `system/openproblems_metrics.py` and `system/openproblems_baselines.json` files. Those should be interesting. So, after the Private Memory Room, we''re returning to the Research Counter to execute those `storage read` commands. Simple enough.

  '
