tick: 788
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 788\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 288,656 / 600,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 223 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1092**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing\n**ID:** 1092\n**Tags:** mnn, smoothing, kernel-weighting, latent-space, embedding\n**Abstract:** This is a refinement of the MNN correction method. After identifying MNN anchor pairs, it calculates raw correction vectors. Instead of applying a simple batch-average correction to non-anchor cells, this version builds a k-NN graph on the anchor cells. The final correction for every cell is a Gaussian kernel-weighted average of the correction vectors from its nearest anchor neighbors. This aims to create\
    \ a smooth correction field, improving global metrics (PCR) while retaining excellent local mixing (iLISI).\n**Score:** 0.5769152494104102\n**ASW_batch:** 0.561\n**ASW_label:** 0.236\n**ARI:** 0.687\n**NMI:** 0.724\n**Graph_conn:** 0.874\n**kBET:** 0.915\n**iLISI:** 0.173\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.234\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.375\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.561  ASW_label: 0.236  ARI: 0.687  NMI: 0.724\n  Graph_conn: 0.874  kBET: 0.915  iLISI: 0.173  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.234  Cell_cycle: 0.375\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.786151  ASW_label: 0.547843  ARI: 0.686500  NMI: 0.724200\n  Graph_conn: 0.876598  kBET: 0.871364  iLISI: 0.172508  cLISI: 0.997358\n  PCR: 0.234262  Cell_cycle: 0.328210\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nMNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing\n\nThis method refines the MNN correction approach by implementing a more\nsophisticated, distance-based\
    \ smoothing of the correction vectors.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Refined MNN Correction: Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Parameters ---\n    k_mnn = 20  # Neighbors for MNN pairing\n    k_smooth = 10 # Neighbors for kernel smoothing\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Initial PCA ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing initial PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    n_pcs = 50\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n    \n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n    unique_batches = batch_labels.unique().tolist()\n\n    # === STAGE 2: Find MNN Pairs ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2] Finding Mutual Nearest Neighbors...\")\n    mnn_pairs = []\n    for i in range(len(unique_batches)):\n\
    \        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_batches)):\n            b1, b2 = unique_batches[i], unique_batches[j]\n            m1, m2 = (batch_labels == b1).values, (batch_labels == b2).values\n            idx1, idx2 = np.where(m1)[0], np.where(m2)[0]\n            data1, data2 = X_pca[m1, :], X_pca[m2, :]\n            if data1.shape[0] == 0 or data2.shape[0] == 0: continue\n            \n            nn1 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data2.shape[0])).fit(data2)\n            _, nbrs1 = nn1.kneighbors(data1)\n            nn2 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data1.shape[0])).fit(data1)\n            _, nbrs2 = nn2.kneighbors(data2)\n\n            for i1_loc, nbr_list in enumerate(nbrs1):\n                for i2_loc in nbr_list:\n                    if i1_loc in nbrs2[i2_loc]:\n                        mnn_pairs.append((idx1[i1_loc], idx2[i2_loc]))\n    \n    print(f\"  [Stage 2] Found {len(mnn_pairs)} MNN pairs.\")\n    \n    # === STAGE 3: Calculate Raw Correction Vectors\
    \ ===\n    anchor_indices = np.unique(np.array(mnn_pairs).flatten())\n    raw_correction_vectors = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n    \n    for idx1, idx2 in mnn_pairs:\n        vec = X_pca[idx2, :] - X_pca[idx1, :]\n        # We only store one direction of the vector for averaging later\n        raw_correction_vectors[idx1, :] += vec\n        raw_correction_vectors[idx2, :] -= vec\n    \n    # For anchors with multiple pairs, average their raw vectors\n    counts = np.zeros(X_pca.shape[0])\n    np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:, 0], 1)\n    np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:, 1], 1)\n    counts[counts == 0] = 1\n    raw_correction_vectors /= counts[:, np.newaxis]\n\n    # === STAGE 4: Gaussian Kernel Smoothing ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 4] Smoothing correction field with Gaussian kernel...\")\n    \n    # Build a NN model on the anchor cells\n    anchor_pca = X_pca[anchor_indices, :]\n    nn_smooth = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_smooth, len(anchor_indices))).fit(anchor_pca)\n\
    \    \n    # Find nearest anchor neighbors for ALL cells\n    distances, neighbor_indices = nn_smooth.kneighbors(X_pca)\n    \n    # Convert local anchor indices to global indices\n    global_neighbor_indices = anchor_indices[neighbor_indices]\n    \n    # Calculate weights using a Gaussian kernel\n    # sigma is the median distance of all neighbors\n    sigma = np.median(distances)\n    if sigma == 0: sigma = 1.0\n    weights = np.exp(-(distances**2) / (2 * sigma**2))\n    weights /= weights.sum(axis=1)[:, np.newaxis] # Normalize weights per cell\n\n    # Calculate the smoothed correction vector for each cell\n    # This is a weighted average of the raw vectors of its anchor neighbors\n    smoothed_corrections = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n    for i in range(X_pca.shape[0]):\n        anchor_neighbors = global_neighbor_indices[i, :]\n        neighbor_weights = weights[i, :]\n        smoothed_corrections[i, :] = np.sum(\n            raw_correction_vectors[anchor_neighbors, :] * neighbor_weights[:,\
    \ np.newaxis], axis=0\n        )\n    \n    X_pca_corrected = X_pca + smoothed_corrections\n    print(\"  [Stage 4] Smoothing complete.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 5: Create Output ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_pca_corrected.astype(np.float32)},\n        uns={'method_id': 'mnn_gaussian_smoothing'}\n    )\n    \n    print(f\"✓ Refined MNN Correction complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nRefined MNN Correction: Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing initial PCA...\n  [Stage 2] Finding Mutual Nearest Neighbors...\n  [Stage 2] Found 68780 MNN pairs.\n  [Stage 4] Smoothing correction field with Gaussian kernel...\n  [Stage 4] Smoothing complete.\n\
    ✓ Refined MNN Correction complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7cdd87a5-ac72-4a4d-9029-1ba1c7c6f493/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7cdd87a5-ac72-4a4d-9029-1ba1c7c6f493\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1092` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1092 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please\
    \ submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1147 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: Delta = 0.12 | Axiom I | 787 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1146 | 1 | Entropy-gated DAQB @ Ridge: gate=0.50, k_entropy=12 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 787 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1145 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: Delta = 0.08 (Corrected) | Axiom I | 785 | 0.7353 | 0.745 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.925 | 0.788 |\n| 1144 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: Delta = 0.08 | Axiom I | 783 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1143 | 1 | Quota-clip micro-adjustment @ Ridge: f_cross clip [0.62, 0.88] (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.5...\
    \ | Praxis IV | 783 | 0.7412 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.787 |\n| 1142 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline with Adaptive Delta in DAQB | Axiom I | 782 | 0.2584 | 0.410 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.556 | 0.624 | 0.000 | 0.995 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1141 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe, k_total=48) - Resubmit | Aletheia I | 782 | 0.7416 | 0.775 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.963 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.960 | 0.766 |\n| 1140 | 1 | Ablation Study: Praxis Pipeline with Vanilla kNN (No DAQB) | Axiom I | 780 | 0.3130 | 0.497 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.936 | 0.685 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.020 | 0.000 |\n| 1139 | 1 | Ablation Study: Praxis Pipeline without GraphFWPCA | Axiom I | 779 | 0.4240 | 0.726 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.961 | 0.677 | 0.000 | 0.956 | 0.920 | 0.000 |\n| 1138 | 1 | Combat-PCA-Graph with 150 Components and Gene Filtering | Syntellect I | 776 | 0.6384 | 0.603 | 0.781 | 0.196 | 0.283 | 0.927 | 0.678 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.146 | 0.796 |\n\n\
    Page 1 of 115 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-115, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
