    \ `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/diagnostics/README.md:**\n```\nRidge Diagnostics and Falsification Kit (Praxis IV, env v4.1)\nContents:\n- ridge_suite.py: Directed-vs-undirected mixing gap, inbound entropy by density, DAQB vs kNN synergy.\n- falsification_kit.py: Two low-coupling probes at the ridge (fixed-k and clip).\n- examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py: Minimal test-only driver that runs the frozen ridge and diagnostics.\n\nUsage in a test-only submission:\n---\nimport sys, anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nfrom diagnostics.ridge_suite import run_all\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_all(adata)\n---\n\nOr run the quickstart that includes the frozen ridge first:\n---\nimport sys, anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nfrom examples.quickstart_ridge_test import test as quickstart\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return quickstart(adata)\n\
    ---\n\nFalsification kit (two probes):\n---\nimport sys, anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nfrom diagnostics.falsification_kit import run_fixed_k_probe, run_clip_probe\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    ad_k = run_fixed_k_probe(adata.copy(), k_variant=52, seed=0)\n    ad_c = run_clip_probe(adata.copy(), clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed=0)\n    print(\"fixed-k shapes:\", ad_k.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_k.obsp['distances'].shape)\n    print(\"clip shapes:\", ad_c.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_c.obsp['distances'].shape)\n    return {\"fixed_k_done\": True, \"clip_done\": True}\n---\n\nNotes:\n- Frozen ridge (current env v4.1 reference): score≈0.7414 with vector\n  [0.659,0.248,0.765,0.725,0.968,0.789,0.961,0.973,1.000,0.327].\n- Runners and modules live under storage/praxis; diagnostics live under storage/shared/diagnostics.\n- Ensure seed=0 for reproducibility; graphs are used as-is by the evaluator.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
