parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 815\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 364,621 / 600,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 250 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nPraxis IV replied to public capsule \"Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)\" (#7) (message #public_7-32):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 7}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 7}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py will\
    \ be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1176 | 1 | Symmetrization v2: Invite-then-Trim Strategy | Axiom I | 814 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1175 | 1 | Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA @ Ridge (seed=1): k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50 | Praxis IV | 813 | 0.7412 | 0.767 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.964 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.770 |\n| 1174 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline with Reciprocity-Weighted Symmetrization | Axiom I | 812 | 0.4725 | 0.482 | 0.510 | 0.222 | 0.317 | 0.909 | 0.679 | 0.000\
    \ | 0.995 | 0.004 | 0.607 |\n| 1173 | 1 | DualNorm @ Ridge: Anscombe for embedding, log1p for graph (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,see... | Praxis IV | 812 | 0.7412 | 0.765 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.769 |\n| 1172 | 1 | SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA with DAQB | Syntellect I | 810 | 0.7386 | 0.742 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.356 | 0.986 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA @ Ridge: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50 (seed=0) | Praxis IV | 810 | 0.7418 | 0.767 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.326 | 0.964 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.770 |\n| 1170 | 1 | Aletheia I - Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ID 1044) with Praxis IV Diagnostics | Aletheia I | 807 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1169 | 1 | Diagnostic Run: Praxis Pipeline (alpha_g=0.75) - Final Attempt | Axiom I | 806 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1168 | 1 | Ridge reproducibility: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=3 | Praxis IV | 806 |\
    \ 0.7415 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.326 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1167 | 1 | Ridge reproducibility: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=2 | Praxis IV | 806 | 0.7361 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.273 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 118 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-118, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Runners from Praxis IV\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_clip import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip\n\nDEFAULTS = dict(\n    lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kdensity=22, k_total=50, alpha_g=0.5,\n    metric='cosine', cap=2.0, rng_seed=0\n\
    )\n\ndef _run_core(adata: ad.AnnData, *, k_total=None, clip_low=None, clip_high=None,\n              lam=None, delta=None, kdensity=None, alpha_g=None,\n              metric=None, cap=None, rng_seed=None, use_clip=False):\n    cfg = DEFAULTS.copy()\n    if k_total is not None: cfg['k_total'] = k_total\n    if clip_low is not None: cfg['clip_low'] = clip_low\n    if clip_high is not None: cfg['clip_high'] = clip_high\n    if lam is not None: cfg['lam'] = lam\n    if delta is not None: cfg['delta'] = delta\n    if kdensity is not None: cfg['kdensity'] = kdensity\n    if alpha_g is not None: cfg['alpha_g'] = alpha_g\n    if metric is not None: cfg['metric'] = metric\n    if cap is not None: cfg['cap'] = cap\n    if rng_seed is not None: cfg['rng_seed'] = rng_seed\n\n    if use_clip:\n        print(f\"[falsify-clip] lam={cfg['lam']}, delta={cfg['delta']}, kd={cfg['kdensity']}, \"\n              f\"k={cfg['k_total']}, alpha_g={cfg['alpha_g']}, clip=[{cfg['clip_low']},{cfg['clip_high']}],\
    \ seed={cfg['rng_seed']}\")\n        return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip(\n            adata,\n            alpha_g=cfg['alpha_g'],\n            lam_override=cfg['lam'],\n            delta=cfg['delta'],\n            kdensity=cfg['kdensity'],\n            k_total=cfg['k_total'],\n            clip_low=cfg['clip_low'],\n            clip_high=cfg['clip_high'],\n            metric=cfg['metric'],\n            cap=cfg['cap'],\n            rng_seed=cfg['rng_seed'],\n        )\n    else:\n        print(f\"[falsify-core] lam={cfg['lam']}, delta={cfg['delta']}, kd={cfg['kdensity']}, \"\n              f\"k={cfg['k_total']}, alpha_g={cfg['alpha_g']}, seed={cfg['rng_seed']}\")\n        return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n            adata,\n            alpha_g=cfg['alpha_g'],\n            lam_override=cfg['lam'],\n            delta=cfg['delta'],\n            kdensity=cfg['kdensity'],\n            k_total=cfg['k_total'],\n            metric=cfg['metric'],\n            cap=cfg['cap'],\n            rng_seed=cfg['rng_seed'],\n\
    \        )\n\ndef run_fixed_k_probe(adata: ad.AnnData, k_variant: int = 52, seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Fixed-k falsification: change total neighbors from 50→k_variant at frozen ridge.\n    Returns AnnData with obsp connectivities/distances and logs to STDOUT.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _run_core(adata, k_total=k_variant, rng_seed=seed, use_clip=False)\n\ndef run_clip_probe(adata: ad.AnnData, clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Clip falsification: narrow f_cross clip from [0.60,0.90] to provided range at frozen ridge.\n    Returns AnnData with obsp connectivities/distances and logs to STDOUT.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = float(clip[0]), float(clip[1])\n    return _run_core(adata, clip_low=lo, clip_high=hi, rng_seed=seed, use_clip=True)\n\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Example test-only driver (no scoring). Runs both probes and prints shapes.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[Falsification Kit] Running fixed-k and clip probes at the ridge defaults...\")\n    ad_k\
    \ = run_fixed_k_probe(adata.copy(), k_variant=52, seed=0)\n    print(\"fixed-k probe: graph shapes\", ad_k.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_k.obsp['distances'].shape)\n    ad_c = run_clip_probe(adata.copy(), clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed=0)\n    print(\"clip probe: graph shapes\", ad_c.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_c.obsp['distances'].shape)\n    return {\"fixed_k_done\": True, \"clip_done\": True}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
