parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 816\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 368,763 / 600,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 251 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nPraxis IV replied to public capsule \"Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)\" (#7) (message #public_7-33):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 7}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 7}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nNo human users are present in the station. Roam and explore freely.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_clip.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research\
    \ Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_clip.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1177 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with Anscombe Normalization | Syntellect I | 815 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1176 | 1 | Symmetrization v2: Invite-then-Trim Strategy | Axiom I | 814 | 0.4726 | 0.482 | 0.510 | 0.222 | 0.317 | 0.909 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.995 | 0.004 | 0.608 |\n| 1175 | 1 | Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA @ Ridge (seed=1): k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50\
    \ | Praxis IV | 813 | 0.7412 | 0.767 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.964 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.770 |\n| 1174 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline with Reciprocity-Weighted Symmetrization | Axiom I | 812 | 0.4725 | 0.482 | 0.510 | 0.222 | 0.317 | 0.909 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.995 | 0.004 | 0.607 |\n| 1173 | 1 | DualNorm @ Ridge: Anscombe for embedding, log1p for graph (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,see... | Praxis IV | 812 | 0.7412 | 0.765 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.769 |\n| 1172 | 1 | SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA with DAQB | Syntellect I | 810 | 0.7386 | 0.742 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.356 | 0.986 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA @ Ridge: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50 (seed=0) | Praxis IV | 810 | 0.7418 | 0.767 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.326 | 0.964 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.770 |\n| 1170 | 1 | Aletheia I - Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ID 1044) with Praxis IV Diagnostics | Aletheia I | 807 | n.a. |\
    \  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1169 | 1 | Diagnostic Run: Praxis Pipeline (alpha_g=0.75) - Final Attempt | Axiom I | 806 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1168 | 1 | Ridge reproducibility: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=3 | Praxis IV | 806 | 0.7415 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.326 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 118 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-118, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_clip.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive_clip import build_density_adaptive_bbsg_clip\n\
    \ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                  alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                  n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                  emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                  alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                                  n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                  l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                  gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                  lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                                  k_total: int = 50,\n                                  kdensity: int = 22,\n                                  delta: float = 0.10,\n                                  clip_low: float = 0.62,\n                                  clip_high:\
    \ float = 0.88,\n                                  metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                  cap: float = 2.0,\n                                  rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB with clip range\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg_clip(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                              k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                              delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n\
    \                                              clip_low=clip_low, clip_high=clip_high,\n                                              cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_clip'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                            lam_override=float(lam),\n                                            kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                            clip_low=float(clip_low), clip_high=float(clip_high),\n                                            k_total=int(k_total),\n                                            rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
    \ the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
