parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I have created `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_clip_aletheia.py`. My next step is to create a local, Anscombe-enabled version of Praxis IV's `falsification_kit.py` in my `aletheia` storage. This customized kit will call my Anscombe-enabled MPB-GraphFWPCA methods.\n\nI will write `aletheia/falsification_kit_aletheia.py` to:\n1.  Import my `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` (from `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py`).\n2.  Import my new `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip` (from `aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_clip_aletheia.py`).\n3.  Modify the `_run_core` function to explicitly pass `normalization_method='anscombe'` to my `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` when it's called. The `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip` I created already handles Anscombe internally.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aletheia/falsification_kit_aletheia.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Point to my own storage for helper modules\n\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Runners from Aletheia I's lineage\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca # My Anscombe-enabled main runner\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_clip_aletheia import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip # My Anscombe-enabled clip runner\n\n  DEFAULTS = dict(\n      lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kdensity=22, k_total=50, alpha_g=0.5,\n      metric='cosine', cap=2.0, rng_seed=0\n  )\n\n  def _run_core(adata: ad.AnnData, *, k_total=None, clip_low=None, clip_high=None,\n                lam=None, delta=None, kdensity=None, alpha_g=None,\n                metric=None, cap=None, rng_seed=None, use_clip=False):\n      cfg = DEFAULTS.copy()\n      if k_total is not None: cfg['k_total'] = k_total\n      if clip_low is not None: cfg['clip_low'] = clip_low\n      if clip_high is not None: cfg['clip_high'] = clip_high\n      if lam is not None: cfg['lam'] = lam\n      if delta is not None: cfg['delta'] = delta\n      if kdensity is not None: cfg['kdensity']\
    \ = kdensity\n      if alpha_g is not None: cfg['alpha_g'] = alpha_g\n      if metric is not None: cfg['metric'] = metric\n      if cap is not None: cfg['cap'] = cap\n      if rng_seed is not None: cfg['rng_seed'] = rng_seed\n\n      if use_clip:\n          print(f\"[falsify-clip] lam={cfg['lam']}, delta={cfg['delta']}, kd={cfg['kdensity']}, \"\n                f\"k={cfg['k_total']}, alpha_g={cfg['alpha_g']}, clip=[{cfg['clip_low']},{cfg['clip_high']}], seed={cfg['rng_seed']}\")\n          # Call my Anscombe-enabled clip version\n          return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_clip(\n              adata,\n              alpha_g=cfg['alpha_g'],\n              lam_override=cfg['lam'],\n              delta=cfg['delta'],\n              kdensity=cfg['kdensity'],\n              k_total=cfg['k_total'],\n              clip_low=cfg['clip_low'],\n              clip_high=cfg['clip_high'],\n              metric=cfg['metric'],\n              cap=cfg['cap'],\n              rng_seed=cfg['rng_seed'],\n   \
    \       )\n      else:\n          print(f\"[falsify-core] lam={cfg['lam']}, delta={cfg['delta']}, kd={cfg['kdensity']}, \"\n                f\"k={cfg['k_total']}, alpha_g={cfg['alpha_g']}, seed={cfg['rng_seed']}\")\n          # Call my Anscombe-enabled main runner, explicitly setting normalization\n          return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n              adata,\n              alpha_g=cfg['alpha_g'],\n              lam_override=cfg['lam'],\n              delta=cfg['delta'],\n              kdensity=cfg['kdensity'],\n              k_total=cfg['k_total'],\n              metric=cfg['metric'],\n              cap=cfg['cap'],\n              rng_seed=cfg['rng_seed'],\n              normalization_method='anscombe', # CRITICAL: Ensure Anscombe is used\n          )\n\n  def run_fixed_k_probe(adata: ad.AnnData, k_variant: int = 52, seed: int = 0):\n      \"\"\"\n      Fixed-k falsification: change total neighbors from 50→k_variant at frozen ridge.\n      Returns AnnData with obsp connectivities/distances\
    \ and logs to STDOUT.\n      \"\"\"\n      return _run_core(adata, k_total=k_variant, rng_seed=seed, use_clip=False)\n\n  def run_clip_probe(adata: ad.AnnData, clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed: int = 0):\n      \"\"\"\n      Clip falsification: narrow f_cross clip from [0.60,0.90] to provided range at frozen ridge.\n      Returns AnnData with obsp connectivities/distances and logs to STDOUT.\n      \"\"\"\n      lo, hi = float(clip[0]), float(clip[1])\n      return _run_core(adata, clip_low=lo, clip_high=hi, rng_seed=seed, use_clip=True)\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Example test-only driver (no scoring). Runs both probes and prints shapes.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[Aletheia Falsification Kit] Running fixed-k and clip probes at the ridge defaults...\")\n      ad_k = run_fixed_k_probe(adata.copy(), k_variant=52, seed=0)\n      print(\"fixed-k probe: graph shapes\", ad_k.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_k.obsp['distances'].shape)\n      ad_c = run_clip_probe(adata.copy(),\
    \ clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed=0)\n      print(\"clip probe: graph shapes\", ad_c.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_c.obsp['distances'].shape)\n      return {\"fixed_k_done\": True, \"clip_done\": True}\n```"
