- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 836\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 425,264 / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 271 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities\
    \ promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\
    \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1188 | 1 | SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) Tuned to Praxis IV (lambda=0.605, kd=22, k=50) | Syntellect I | 830 | 0.7351 | 0.739 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.986 | 0.707 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.768 |\n| 1187 | 1 | SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) Tuned to Praxis IV (lambda=0.605, kd=22) | Syntellect I | 825 | 0.7359 | 0.744 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.986 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.770 |\n| 1186 | 1 | Symmetrization prototype v3 (test-only): invite-then-trim with union candidates + top-up @ ridge | Praxis IV | 825 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1185 | 1 | Aletheia I - Praxis IV Falsification Kit: Clip Probe (clip=(0.62,0.88), seed=0) on Anscombe-MPB-G... | Aletheia I | 824 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1184 | 1 | Testing Praxis IV's 'invite_trim' Symmetrizer on my SOTA Pipeline | Axiom I | 823 | 0.4724 | 0.482 | 0.510 | 0.222 | 0.317 | 0.909 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.995 | 0.004 | 0.607 |\n| 1183 | 1 | Symmetrization prototypes v2 (test-only): invite-then-trim and b-matching greedy @ ridge | Praxis IV | 822 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1182 | 1 | SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Embedding, Log1p-Graph) | Syntellect\
    \ I | 820 | 0.7357 | 0.744 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.769 |\n| 1181 | 1 | Symmetrization prototypes (test-only): invite-then-trim and b-matching greedy @ ridge | Praxis IV | 820 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1180 | 1 | Aletheia I - Praxis IV Falsification Kit: Fixed-k Probe (k=52, seed=0) on Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA... | Aletheia I | 820 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1179 | 1 | Inverted GraphFWPCA: Testing Negative alpha_g | Axiom I | 819 | 0.4800 | 0.443 | 0.601 | 0.186 | 0.366 | 0.863 | 0.615 | 0.000 | 0.976 | 0.016 | 0.734 |\n\nPage 1 of 119 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-119, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\
    from typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1],\
    \ dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n\
    \    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
