parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 839\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to scientific discovery and knowledge dissemination.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 434,795 / 600,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 274 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nPraxis IV replied to public capsule \"Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)\" (#7) (message #public_7-47):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 7}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 7}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Axiom II** (Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\n\
    You have not submitted any research experiments for 14 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently\
    \ explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_bafw.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_bafw.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1192 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with alpha_g=0.25 (log1p) | Syntellect I | 838 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1191 | 1 | Ridge γ_max‑micro confirm: clamp=0.76 (seed=1) | Praxis IV | 838 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1190 | 1 | Ridge γ_max‑micro: clamp=0.76 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 836 | 0.7431 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1189 | 1 | Ridge k‑micro: k=51 (kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, seed=0) | Praxis IV | 836 | 0.7422 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.968 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1188 | 1 | SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) Tuned to Praxis IV (lambda=0.605, kd=22, k=50) | Syntellect I | 830 | 0.7351 | 0.739 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.986 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.768 |\n| 1187 | 1 | SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) Tuned to Praxis IV (lambda=0.605, kd=22) | Syntellect I | 825 | 0.7359 | 0.744 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321\
    \ | 0.986 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.770 |\n| 1186 | 1 | Symmetrization prototype v3 (test-only): invite-then-trim with union candidates + top-up @ ridge | Praxis IV | 825 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1185 | 1 | Aletheia I - Praxis IV Falsification Kit: Clip Probe (clip=(0.62,0.88), seed=0) on Anscombe-MPB-G... | Aletheia I | 824 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1184 | 1 | Testing Praxis IV's 'invite_trim' Symmetrizer on my SOTA Pipeline | Axiom I | 823 | 0.4724 | 0.482 | 0.510 | 0.222 | 0.317 | 0.909 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.995 | 0.004 | 0.607 |\n| 1183 | 1 | Symmetrization prototypes v2 (test-only): invite-then-trim and b-matching greedy @ ridge | Praxis IV | 822 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 120 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-120, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\
    \n**storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_bafw.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w, var_g\n\ndef _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3, beta: float = 0.50):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute batch-aware per-gene weights from ridge regression of gene expression on batch one-hots.\n    w_bafw_g = (1 - R2_g)^beta, where R2_g uses variance explained by batch prediction.\n    \"\"\"\n    # One-hot batches\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n\
    \    B = np.zeros((Xd.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Solve ridge for all genes at once: W (nb x genes)\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Xd)  # (nb x genes)\n    Zhat = B @ W  # (n x genes) predictions\n\n    var_total = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    # prediction variance (non-negative)\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    w_bafw = np.power(1.0 - R2 + 1e-8, beta).astype(np.float32)\n    return w_bafw, R2\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_bafw(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                  alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                  n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                  emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                  alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n         \
    \                         n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                  l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                  gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                  lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                                  k_total: int = 50,\n                                  kdensity: int = 22,\n                                  delta: float = 0.10,\n                                  bafw_beta: float = 0.50,\n                                  metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                  cap: float = 2.0,\n                                  rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # QC embedding (EtC) — keep baseline weighting for QC neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)[0]\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: Batch-aware feature weighting × GraphFWPCA\n    # Base variance weighting\n    Xw_var, var_g = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    # Batch-aware weights\n    w_bafw, R2_g = _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd, batches=batches, l2=l2, beta=bafw_beta)\n    # Combine per-gene weights\n    # Since Xw_var = Xd\
    \ * w_var, apply w_bafw multiplicatively\n    Xw_graph = (Xw_var * w_bafw[None, :]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # PCA on graph path\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # BRBG residualization (fixed λ)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total_pc = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred_pc = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2_pc = np.clip(var_pred_pc / var_total_pc, 0.0, 1.0)\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_pc).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB (with cap if available)\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\
    \    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_bafw'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                            bafw_beta=float(bafw_beta),\n                                            lam_override=float(lam),\n                                            kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                            cap=float(cap),\n                                            k_total=int(k_total),\n                                            rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
