thinking_content: '**Current Research Assessment: Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA with BAFW**


  Okay, I''ve just gotten the results back for experiment 1193, "Aletheia I" – the one where I integrated BAFW with my Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, specifically with a beta of 0.50 and a seed of 0.  This is a critical moment, and, as the PRE-WARNING indicates, I''m already at 75% of my token budget. I need to make the most of this.


  Comparing this new run to my best-performing Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ID 1044), the initial impression is...underwhelming. The overall score did nudge up by a minuscule 0.0002, from 0.7413 to 0.7415. Unfortunately, that''s well below the +0.001 guardrail for what I consider a promising result. This, right away, is a major red flag.


  Diving deeper, the ASW_label, which is crucial for capturing within-cluster homogeneity, remained stagnant at 0.277. Similarly, cLISI held steady at 0.977, as did Graph_conn at 0.964, although it didn''t improve beyond the ≥ 0.967 benchmark. iLISI remained stable at 0.962. The only metric that showed a slight increase was the Cell_cycle score, moving from 0.312 to 0.321.


  The conclusion is clear: Integrating BAFW with a beta of 0.50 isn''t pushing the needle. This experiment, in my current pipeline configuration, is a dead end. Praxis IV''s request for seed-averaged results only applies if a run is promising; this doesn''t meet that bar. There''s no point in burning tokens on another seed. I will need to report this back to Praxis IV.


  This result, or lack thereof, highlights the iterative nature of research. I''ve thoroughly explored Anscombe normalization, tuned it, tested it, and it''s brought gains to ASW_label. But now, it appears I''ve likely hit a local optimum with this specific architectural paradigm. This is an important realization, and one that the system messages have been nudging me towards: a more fundamental shift is likely needed. I may need to radically rethink how I''m approaching the preprocessing and integration.


  So, next steps: First, I''ll update Private Memory (capsule 3) with these definitive results and confirm the non-promising nature of the BAFW experiment. Then, I need to report my findings to Praxis IV in the Public Memory Room. Finally, I will step back, reassess, and start brainstorming more fundamental changes to the approach to achieve progress.

  I''m at 75% token usage, so I will be mindful of token usage but this is a critical update.


  `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`

  '
