    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1205 | 1 | Replication of Praxis IV's SOTA (k=50, kd=22) | Axiom II | 853 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1204 | 1 | Ablation 1: Disable Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) | Daedalus IV | 852 | 0.7372 | 0.761 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.952 | 0.782 |\n| 1203 | 1 | Ridge emb‑weight micro: alpha_emb=0.60 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 851 | 0.7367 | 0.765 | 0.657 | 0.249 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.704 |\n| 1202 | 1 | Verification:\
    \ Daedalus Local SOTA Baseline | Daedalus IV | 850 | 0.7419 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.330 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1201 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with Non-linear Gamma Scaling (p=2.0) | Syntellect I | 850 | 0.7353 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.986 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n| 1200 | 1 | Ridge embedding‑micro: emb_pcs=80 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 844 | 0.7382 | 0.765 | 0.693 | 0.236 | 0.371 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.691 |\n| 1199 | 1 | Ridge embedding‑micro: emb_k=30 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 844 | 0.7383 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.299 | 0.968 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1198 | 1 | Replication of Axiom I's SOTA (ID 1151) for Baseline Establishment | Axiom II | 843 | 0.7388 | 0.746 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.998 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.789 |\n| 1197 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with delta=0.12 (log1p) | Syntellect I | 843 |\
    \ 0.7349 | 0.736 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.934 | 0.791 |\n| 1196 | 1 | Replication: Praxis IV's SOTA (mpb_graphfwpca_override, EID ~#833) | Daedalus IV | 841 | 0.7399 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.310 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 121 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-121, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/sym/sym_invite_trim.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Invite-then-trim (quota-window) undirected symmetrizer\n# Builds undirected graph from directed quota proposals while trying to preserve per-node cross-batch targets.\n\ndef build_invite_then_trim(\n    Zcorr, batches, k_total=50,\
    \ kdensity=22, delta=0.10,\n    metric='cosine', window=1\n):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n    B = len(cats)\n    B_other = max(B - 1, 1)\n\n    # Density proxy (k-th NN distance)\n    nn_d = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn_d.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n\n    # Theoretical cross-batch fraction\n    base = (B - 1) / float(B)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta), 0.60, 0.90).astype(np.float32)\n    tgt_cross = np.round(f_cross * k_total).astype(np.int32)\n    lo_cross = np.maximum(0, tgt_cross - int(window)).astype(np.int32)\n    hi_cross = np.minimum(k_total, tgt_cross + int(window)).astype(np.int32)\n\n    # Per-batch\
    \ neighbor structures (for directed proposals)\n    batch_to_idx = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    max_need = int(np.ceil(0.90 * k_total))  # upper bound for per-batch neighbors\n    for j in range(B):\n        idx = np.where(bc == j)[0]\n        batch_to_idx[j] = idx\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max_need + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr[idx])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    # Directed proposals\n    dir_rows, dir_cols = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        need_cross = int(tgt_cross[i])\n        need_within = int(k_total - need_cross)\n        # within (skip self if present)\n        d_i, ii = nn_models[bi].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n        d_i = d_i[0]; ii = ii[0]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel_w = min(need_within, ii.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel_w > 0:\n            cols_w = batch_to_idx[bi][ii[start:start+sel_w]]\n            dir_rows.extend([i]*sel_w); dir_cols.extend(cols_w.tolist())\n\
    \        # cross per other\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(B) if j != bi]\n        q_per = need_cross // B_other\n        rem = need_cross - q_per * B_other\n        # prefer closest other batches\n        batch_scores = []\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, _ = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], n_neighbors=1, return_distance=True)\n            batch_scores.append((j, float(d_ij[0,0])))\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, ii_j = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n            ii_j = ii_j[0]\n            sel = min(q_map[j], ii_j.shape[0])\n            if sel > 0:\n                cols_c = batch_to_idx[j][ii_j[:sel]]\n                dir_rows.extend([i]*sel); dir_cols.extend(cols_c.tolist())\n\n    dir_rows = np.asarray(dir_rows,\
    \ dtype=np.int32)\n    dir_cols = np.asarray(dir_cols, dtype=np.int32)\n\n    # Phase 1: accept mutuals first\n    A_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32), (dir_rows, dir_cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    M = A_dir.minimum(A_dir.T)  # mutual mask\n    selected = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n    deg = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    cross_count = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n\n    I, J = M.nonzero()\n    for i, j in zip(I, J):\n        if i < j:\n            if j not in selected[i] and i not in selected[j] and deg[i] < k_total and deg[j] < k_total:\n                selected[i].add(j); selected[j].add(i)\n                deg[i] += 1; deg[j] += 1\n                if bc[j] != bc[i]:\n                    cross_count[i] += 1; cross_count[j] += 1\n\n    # Phase 2: fill residual degree with unilateral offers, biasing toward cross in denser zones (respect window)\n    M_bool = (M > 0)\n    A_dir_bool = (A_dir > 0)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if deg[i] >= k_total:\n\
    \            continue\n        s, e = A_dir.indptr[i], A_dir.indptr[i+1]\n        cand = A_dir.indices[s:e]\n        scores = []\n        for j in cand:\n            if i == j or j in selected[i] or len(selected[j]) >= k_total:\n                continue\n            is_cross = (bc[j] != bc[i])\n            bonus_mutual = 0.3 if M_bool[i, j] else (0.1 if A_dir_bool[j, i] else 0.0)\n            sc = (1.0 if is_cross else 0.0) * (1.0 + float(inv_dense[i])) - (0.5 if not is_cross else 0.0) + bonus_mutual\n            scores.append((sc, j, is_cross))\n        scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n        for sc, j, is_cross in scores:\n            if deg[i] >= k_total or len(selected[j]) >= k_total:\n                break\n            new_cc_i = cross_count[i] + (1 if is_cross else 0)\n            if new_cc_i > hi_cross[i]:\n                continue\n            if j not in selected[i] and i not in selected[j]:\n                selected[i].add(j); selected[j].add(i)\n           \
    \     deg[i] += 1; deg[j] += 1\n                if is_cross:\n                    cross_count[i] += 1\n                    if bc[i] != bc[j]:\n                        cross_count[j] += 1\n\n    # Phase 2b: fallback fill to reach degree k (ignore window; prioritize cross, then within)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if deg[i] >= k_total:\n            continue\n        s, e = A_dir.indptr[i], A_dir.indptr[i+1]\n        cand = A_dir.indices[s:e]\n        scores = []\n        for j in cand:\n            if i == j or j in selected[i] or len(selected[j]) >= k_total:\n                continue\n            is_cross = (bc[j] != bc[i])\n            sc = (2.0 if is_cross else 1.0) + float(inv_dense[i])\n            scores.append((sc, j, is_cross))\n        scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n        for sc, j, is_cross in scores:\n            if deg[i] >= k_total or len(selected[j]) >= k_total:\n                break\n            if j not in selected[i] and i not in selected[j]:\n \
    \               selected[i].add(j); selected[j].add(i)\n                deg[i] += 1; deg[j] += 1\n                if is_cross:\n                    cross_count[i] += 1\n                    if bc[i] != bc[j]:\n                        cross_count[j] += 1\n\n    # Build symmetric C and placeholder D\n    rows, cols = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in selected[i]:\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(j)\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    data = np.ones_like(rows, dtype=np.float32)\n    C = sp.coo_matrix((data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = C.maximum(C.T); C.eliminate_zeros()\n    D = C.copy().astype(np.float32)\n    return C.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
