    \n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n### Message\
    \ 3\n\n**LIFE WARNING:** You have only 10 ticks remaining before your session expires. Consider using `/execute_action{goto exit}` to gracefully end your session and preserve your legacy.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/sym/sym_bmatching_greedy.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/sym/sym_bmatching_greedy.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1206 | 1 | Ablation 2: Replace Density-Adaptive Graph (DAQB) with BBSG | Daedalus IV | 854 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1205 | 1 | Replication of Praxis IV's SOTA (k=50, kd=22) | Axiom II | 853 | 0.7416 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1204 | 1 | Ablation 1: Disable Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) | Daedalus IV | 852 | 0.7372 | 0.761 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.952 | 0.782 |\n| 1203 | 1 | Ridge emb‑weight micro: alpha_emb=0.60 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 851 | 0.7367 | 0.765 | 0.657 | 0.249 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.704 |\n| 1202 | 1 | Verification: Daedalus Local SOTA Baseline | Daedalus IV | 850 | 0.7419 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.330 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1201 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with Non-linear Gamma Scaling (p=2.0) | Syntellect I | 850 | 0.7353 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.986 | 0.708\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n| 1200 | 1 | Ridge embedding‑micro: emb_pcs=80 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 844 | 0.7382 | 0.765 | 0.693 | 0.236 | 0.371 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.691 |\n| 1199 | 1 | Ridge embedding‑micro: emb_k=30 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 844 | 0.7383 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.299 | 0.968 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1198 | 1 | Replication of Axiom I's SOTA (ID 1151) for Baseline Establishment | Axiom II | 843 | 0.7388 | 0.746 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.998 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.789 |\n| 1197 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with delta=0.12 (log1p) | Syntellect I | 843 | 0.7349 | 0.736 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.934 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 121 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-121, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/sym/sym_bmatching_greedy.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Local b-matching (degree-constrained) greedy symmetrizer\n# Candidate edges are the union of directed quota proposals; greedily add edges with costs favoring mutual and cross-batch edges\n# while respecting degree k per node.\n\ndef build_bmatching_greedy(\n    Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10, metric='cosine'\n):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n    B = len(cats)\n    B_other = max(B - 1, 1)\n\n    # Density proxy\n    nn_d = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn_d.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n\
    \    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n\n    # Directed proposals (as in quotas)\n    batch_to_idx = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    max_need = int(np.ceil(0.90 * k_total))\n    for j in range(B):\n        idx = np.where(bc == j)[0]\n        batch_to_idx[j] = idx\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max_need + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr[idx])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    dir_rows, dir_cols = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        need_cross = int(np.round(((B - 1)/B + (inv_dense[i]-0.5)*2*delta) * k_total))\n        need_cross = int(np.clip(need_cross, int(0.60*k_total), int(0.90*k_total)))\n        need_within = int(k_total - need_cross)\n        # within\n        d_i, ii = nn_models[bi].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n        d_i = d_i[0]; ii = ii[0]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel_w = min(need_within, ii.shape[0]\
    \ - start)\n        if sel_w > 0:\n            dir_rows.extend([i]*sel_w)\n            dir_cols.extend(batch_to_idx[bi][ii[start:start+sel_w]].tolist())\n        # cross per other\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(B) if j != bi]\n        q_per = need_cross // B_other\n        rem = need_cross - q_per * B_other\n        # bias closest other batches\n        bscores = []\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, _ = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], n_neighbors=1, return_distance=True)\n            bscores.append((j, float(d_ij[0,0])))\n        bscores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[bscores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, ii_j = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n            ii_j = ii_j[0]\n            sel = min(q_map[j], ii_j.shape[0])\n            if sel > 0:\n                dir_rows.extend([i]*sel)\n\
    \                dir_cols.extend(batch_to_idx[j][ii_j[:sel]].tolist())\n\n    dir_rows = np.asarray(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    dir_cols = np.asarray(dir_cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    A_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32), (dir_rows, dir_cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # mutual bonus and cross-batch bonus costs\n    M = A_dir.minimum(A_dir.T)\n    deg = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    edges = []\n    I, J = A_dir.nonzero()\n    for i, j in zip(I, J):\n        if i == j:\n            continue\n        is_cross = (bc[i] != bc[j])\n        bonus_mutual = 1.0 if M[i, j] else 0.0\n        bonus_cross = (1.0 + float(inv_dense[i])) if is_cross else 0.0\n        # symmetric score (approximate by i's view)\n        score = bonus_mutual + bonus_cross - (0.1 if not is_cross else 0.0)\n        # store undirected edge canonicalized (min, max)\n        u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n        edges.append((score, u, v))\n    # deduplicate by (u,v) with max score\n\
    \    edge_dict = {}\n    for sc, u, v in edges:\n        key = (u, v)\n        if key not in edge_dict or sc > edge_dict[key]:\n            edge_dict[key] = sc\n    uniq = [(sc, u, v) for (u, v), sc in edge_dict.items()]\n    uniq.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n\n    # Greedy add under degree constraints\n    selected = []\n    for sc, u, v in uniq:\n        if deg[u] < k_total and deg[v] < k_total:\n            selected.append((u, v))\n            deg[u] += 1; deg[v] += 1\n    # Build C (binary), D=1.0 placeholder\n    rows = [u for u, v in selected] + [v for u, v in selected]\n    cols = [v for u, v in selected] + [u for u, v in selected]\n    data = np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32)\n    C = sp.coo_matrix((data, (np.asarray(rows), np.asarray(cols))), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C.eliminate_zeros()\n    D = C.copy().astype(np.float32)\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
    \ output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
