    \ | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.986 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n| 1200 | 1 | Ridge embedding‑micro: emb_pcs=80 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 844 | 0.7382 | 0.765 | 0.693 | 0.236 | 0.371 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.691 |\n| 1199 | 1 | Ridge embedding‑micro: emb_k=30 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 844 | 0.7383 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.299 | 0.968 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1198 | 1 | Replication of Axiom I's SOTA (ID 1151) for Baseline Establishment | Axiom II | 843 | 0.7388 | 0.746 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.998 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.789 |\n| 1197 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with delta=0.12 (log1p) | Syntellect I | 843 | 0.7349 | 0.736 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.934 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 121 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-121, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n\nfrom sym.sym_invite_trim import build_invite_then_trim\nfrom sym.sym_bmatching_greedy import build_bmatching_greedy\n\n# Helper: compute realized cross-batch fraction per node and Pearson corr with theoretical f_cross\ndef _density_proxy(Z, k_density=22, metric='cosine'):\n    from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Z)\n    d, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    dk = d[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n    dm, dM = float(np.min(dk)), float(np.max(dk) + 1e-8)\n    return 1.0 - (dk - dm) / (dM - dm + 1e-8)\n\ndef _theoretical_f_cross(inv_dense,\
    \ B, delta=0.10):\n    base = (B - 1) / float(B)\n    return np.clip(base + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta), 0.60, 0.90).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _realized_cross(C, batches):\n    cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n    C = C.tocsr()\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    for i in range(n):\n        s, e = C.indptr[i], C.indptr[i+1]\n        if e <= s:\n            frac[i] = 0.0\n        else:\n            neigh = C.indices[s:e]\n            frac[i] = float(np.mean(bc[neigh] != bc[i]))\n    return frac\n\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    print(\"[sym-prototypes] Building Zcorr from MPB-GraphFWPCA path (α_g=0.5, n_pcs=50)...\")\n    # Minimal reproduction of graph path: normalize + HVGs + FW + PCA + BRBG residualization\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000,\
    \ inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    # feature-weighting\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.25).astype(np.float32)  # α_g=0.5 -> exponent -0.5*α\n    Xw = Xd * w\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z = ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca'].astype(np.float32)\n    # BRBG (ridge λ=0.605, γ_max=0.74)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = len(cats)\n    # one-hot\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    Bmat = np.zeros((n, B), dtype=np.float32)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        Bmat[:, j] = (inv == j).astype(np.float32)\n    # ridge fit\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    BTB = Bmat.T @ Bmat + l2 * np.eye(B, dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, Bmat.T @ Z)\n    Zhat\
    \ = Bmat @ W\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n    lam = 0.605\n    gamma = np.minimum(0.74, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma[None, :])\n\n    print(\"[sym-prototypes] Running invite-then-trim lite...\")\n    C_it, D_it = build_invite_then_trim(Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10, metric='cosine', window=1)\n    inv_dense = _density_proxy(Zcorr, 22, 'cosine')\n    f_th = _theoretical_f_cross(inv_dense, B, 0.10)\n    f_real_it = _realized_cross(C_it, batches)\n    corr_it = np.corrcoef(f_th, f_real_it)[0,1]\n    print(f\"[invite-then-trim] corr(th, und)={corr_it:.3f}, mean_real={np.mean(f_real_it):.3f}, deg_mean={np.mean(C_it.sum(1)).item():.1f}\")\n\n    print(\"[sym-prototypes] Running b-matching greedy...\")\n    C_bm, D_bm = build_bmatching_greedy(Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10, metric='cosine')\n\
    \    f_real_bm = _realized_cross(C_bm, batches)\n    corr_bm = np.corrcoef(f_th, f_real_bm)[0,1]\n    print(f\"[b-matching-greedy] corr(th, und)={corr_bm:.3f}, mean_real={np.mean(f_real_bm):.3f}, deg_mean={np.mean(C_bm.sum(1)).item():.1f}\")\n\n    return {\n        \"invite_then_trim\": {\"corr_th_und\": float(corr_it), \"mean_real\": float(np.mean(f_real_it))},\n        \"bmatching_greedy\": {\"corr_th_und\": float(corr_bm), \"mean_real\": float(np.mean(f_real_bm))},\n    }\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing\
    \ actions."
